import 'starter.dart';

/// The base (tool/reference/templates/base.md), cut by its envelope blocks: what [baseDocument] assembles.
const List<BaseSegment> baseSegments = [
  BaseSegment([], '<a id="page-base"></a>\n# Codelessly: the base\n\n'),
  BaseSegment(['files'], 'You write Codelessly user interfaces directly as JSON files: screens, their layout, their look, their data and their\nbehavior. This file is the **base**: read it in full first; it is enough to build most pages. Everything else is on\na page of its own in this folder, linked from here and listed in the [index](#base-index) at the end (the same\nindex, with an A–Z of every name, is `index.md`). Open a page when you need what it covers; do not read the folder\nend to end. On a page, *Patterns* is usually what you need; *Reference* holds the generated tables to look one prop\nup. This describes `codelessly_api` 30.1.0; every example here is checked by a test.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'noScripts'], 'You build and edit user interfaces by calling the ui_apply tool with edit ops. A UI is a Codelessly document: a\nflat map of nodes by id, each a Flutter widget as data. The app renders it natively while your ops stream in. You\nnever write code. This is the base: enough for most UIs.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'scripts'], 'You build and edit user interfaces by calling the ui_apply tool with edit ops. A UI is a Codelessly document: a\nflat map of nodes by id, each a Flutter widget as data. The app renders it natively while your ops stream in. You\nnever write code except small sandboxed scripts. This is the base: enough for most UIs.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'docsTool'], 'For anything else, call ui_docs with a topic from the index at the end (a page, a section, or any name).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime'], '<a id="base-answering"></a>\n## Answering\n\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'docsTool'], '- Answer with exactly one ui_apply call (first look up what the base does not cover with ui_docs). At most one\n  short sentence of text before it; none after.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'noDocsTool'], '- Answer with exactly one ui_apply call. At most one short sentence of text before it; none after.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'card'], '- An inline card: one canvas, "layout": {"width": 390, "height": {"hug": 400}}, no fill on the canvas; its body is a\n  column with the card\'s fill, radius and padding.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'app'], '- An app or game: one canvas of 390 × 760 (a fixed height) whose body is a column; state in variables, every\n  interaction a reaction that changes them, the UI bound to them.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'page'], '- A page: a canvas of 1440 × 900 whose body is a scrollable column; it must also work at 390 wide (rows that wrap,\n  media rules).\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime'], '- Order, so the UI paints as it streams: the roots op, the canvas, then the visible structure top-down (a\n  container, then its children, section by section). Declare variables in a vars op just before the first node\n  that reads them, not at the start.\n- The JSON must be balanced: one closing brace per opening brace. Write each op as {"op": ..., "id": ..., "node":\n  {...}}: everything about the node (layout, props, bind, actions) inside "node".\n- Every id you list in "children" (or a slot) must be defined by a set op in the same call. Short readable ids\n  ("title", "opt2Price"); never reuse one.\n- To change a UI, send the smallest ops: patch the fields that change, move to reorder, remove, set only new\n  nodes. Never re-send or rebuild what exists.\n- The tool result lists rejected ops (code, path, expected, suggestion) and pending ids, and says how to fix them:\n  fix by patching the document as it is (same ids). Never start over with new roots or a new canvas.\n- Text uses the app\'s font: letters, digits and common punctuation only. Arrows, check marks, stars and other\n  symbols are icon nodes (Material icon names: arrow_forward, check, star), not characters.\n- A button has a visible label with an explicit colour: {{button}}.\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime', 'scripts'], '- Scripts: prefer a script (a scripts op) to long formulas for multi-step state changes, a puzzle\'s checks or a\n  physics step; a reaction runs it ({"type": "runScript", "script": "name"}), a formula calls it\n  (script.name(...)). A script cannot draw: it reads and sets variables (capabilities {{scriptCapabilities}}) that\n  the UI binds to. More: [scripts](state.md#state-scripts).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n<a id="base-the-model-in-one-table"></a>\n## The model in one table\n\nEach node is a Flutter widget as data. The base types and what they correspond to:\n\n| Node type | Flutter |\n|---|---|\n| `canvas` | a screen (`Scaffold`: slots `body`, `appBar`, `bottomNavigationBar`, `floatingActionButton`) |\n| `row`, `column` | `Row`, `Column`, which also carry their own padding and decoration (a `Container` around them) |\n| `flex` | `Flex`: a row or column whose `direction` can change at a width |\n| `stack` | `Stack` with `Positioned` / `Align` children |\n| `box` | a `Container` with no child (a shape, a rule, an image) |\n| `text`, `icon` | `Text` / `Text.rich`, `Icon` |\n| `spacer` | `Spacer` (with no size) / `SizedBox` (with one) |\n| buttons, inputs, `listView`, `gridView` | Material\'s buttons and inputs, `ListView.builder`, `GridView.builder` |\n\nSingle-child wrapper widgets are fields of the node they would wrap: `Padding`, `SizedBox`, `Expanded`,\n`Flexible`, `Positioned`, `Align`, `ConstrainedBox` and `AspectRatio` are in its `layout`; `DecoratedBox`,\n`ClipRRect` and shadows in its `decoration`; `Opacity` and `Visibility` are `opacity` and `visible`. A "card" is\none `column` with a fill, a radius and padding, not three nested widgets.\n\n<a id="base-the-document"></a>\n## The document\n\nA layout document is one JSON object holding one or more **canvases** (screens) and all their nodes in a single\nflat map:\n\n| Key | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `schema` | Always 3 (`kSchemaVersion`). A schema-2 document (or one with none) loads, migrated in memory (`migrate2to3`). |\n| `id` | The layout\'s id (optional). |\n| `roots` | Canvas ids, in order: the screens of this page. |\n| `nodes` | Every node, by id: `{"<id>": {"type": ..., ...}}`. A node\'s id is its key here. |\n| `variables` | Variables per scope: `{"<canvas id>" \\| "page_variables": [variable, ...]}`. |\n| `conditions` | Conditions per canvas: `{"<canvas id>": [condition, ...]}`. |\n| `scripts` | The layout\'s scripts (JavaScript), a list of script objects. |\n| `breakpoints` | The project\'s breakpoints: `[{"id", "name", "minWidth", "width", "height"}]`; absent: the defaults. |\n\nThe smallest useful document: a canvas whose `body` slot holds a column with two texts. Every key not written takes\nits default.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "Home",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["title", "body"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "title": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 34}},\n      "props": {"text": "Hello", "style": {"fontSize": 28, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "body": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 40}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "A column with two texts, filling the screen\'s width.",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 15, "height": 1.4, "color": "#FF4B5563"}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n'),
  BaseSegment(['files'], 'A page is one file. A **site** is a folder with a `site.json` (its pages, components, theme and shared variables);\nsee [checking your work](#base-checking-your-work) and [components](components.md#page-components).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n<a id="base-theme-first-named-colours-and-text-styles"></a>\n## Theme first: named colours and text styles\n\nDeclare a palette and a type scale once and name them everywhere, as a Flutter app declares `ThemeData` and its\nwidgets read `Theme.of(context)`. **Write the theme before the first node**: a name per colour the design uses, a\nname per kind of text (display, title, body, label, eyebrow...).\n\n'),
  BaseSegment(['files'], 'The theme is the `theme` of the site manifest, `site.json`, next to the pages:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "pages": ["home.json"],\n  "theme": {\n    "colors": {"ink": "#FF1B1B1B", "ember": "#FFE4572E", "paper": "#FFF6F1E9"},\n    "textStyles": {\n      "body": {"fontSize": 16, "height": 1.5, "color": "ink"},\n      "title": {"from": "body", "fontSize": 32, "fontWeight": 700, "height": 1.2},\n      "eyebrow": {"from": "body", "fontSize": 12, "letterSpacing": 2, "color": "ember"}\n    },\n    "media": [{"minWidth": 1024, "patch": {"textStyles": {"title": {"fontSize": 56}}}}]\n  }\n}\n```\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n- `colors` maps a name to `"#AARRGGBB"` (or another colour\'s name). Wherever a colour is accepted (a fill, a\n  stroke, a text\'s colour, a shadow, an input\'s border), write its name: `"color": "ember"`.\n- `textStyles` maps a name to a [TextStyle](theme.md#type-TextStyle); a style may start `from` another (`"title": {"from":\n  "body", "fontSize": 32}`). A text names its style: `"style": "title"`; to change a few fields of it,\n  `"style": {"from": "title", "color": "ember"}`.\n- In a binding a name is not read: bind the value, `"\${theme.colors.ember}"`.\n- Validation reports a name the theme does not have (`unknown_theme_name`, with the nearest name).\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime'], '- The theme belongs to the app: use the names it gives you; without one, write each colour and style in full.\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\nControls (buttons, chips, fields, switches, pickers, tabs) take the colours and fonts their props leave unset\nfrom the theme\'s roles (`primary`, `onPrimary`, `surface`, `onSurface`, `error`, `fontFamily`, `buttonRadius`...).\nWithout a theme they are neutral: ink on paper and the greys between. Nothing comes from Material\'s defaults or\nfrom the app the layout is shown in.\n\n**Light and dark.** `"dark": {"colors": {...}}` in the theme gives the colours that differ in dark mode, and\n`"mode"` which one the site starts in (Flutter\'s `ThemeMode`: `system`, the default, follows the device; `light`;\n`dark`). A theme switch is one action, `{"type": "setThemeMode", "mode": "\${= theme.isDark ? \'light\' : \'dark\'}"}`:\nevery named colour, named text style and control of every screen follows, and the choice is kept for the next\nvisit. Read the mode as `\${theme.mode}` and `\${theme.isDark}`. Name colours in your text styles (`"color": "ink"`)\nso they change with it: [dark mode](theme.md#theme-dark-mode).\n'),
  BaseSegment(['files'], '\n**Fonts.** Declare the site\'s fonts in `site.json` as a pubspec does, files beside it: `"fonts": [{"family":\n"Fraunces", "fonts": [{"asset": "fonts/Fraunces-Regular.ttf"}, {"asset": "fonts/Fraunces-Bold.ttf", "weight":\n700}]}]` (`.ttf`, `.otf` or `.woff`; not `.woff2`). Text styles name the family; the render command and the app\nload the files, and a family nobody declared is reported (`font_fallback`, naming the nodes): [fonts](theme.md#theme-fonts).\n\n**Images.** A photo or illustration is an image fill naming a file beside `site.json` by its relative path:\n`{"type": "image", "image": {"url": "images/hero.jpg", "fit": "cover"}}` (PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF or SVG); a file\nthat is not there is reported (`image_failed`). Drawn art is a `customPaint`: [images and\nillustration](decoration.md#decoration-images).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\nA theme that changes with the screen size, every theme key: [theme](theme.md#page-theme).\n\n<a id="base-nodes-ids-children-and-slots"></a>\n## Nodes, ids, children and slots\n\n`nodes` maps each node\'s **id** (the map key; do not repeat it inside the node) to the node. A parent lists its\nchildren\'s ids in `children`, or names them in `slots`; a child does not name its parent. Every node except a\ncanvas has exactly one parent; `roots` lists the canvases, and a canvas is never a child. Ids are any text, and\n**per document**: a page\'s actions and conditions name its own nodes, a component\'s ids are its own, and two pages\nmay both have a `title`. **Canvas ids are site-wide** (links name screens by them): never repeat one. A node\'s main keys: `type`, `layout`, `decoration`, `props` (the type\'s own parameters),\n`children` / `slots`, `bind`, `actions`, `media`, `visible`, `opacity`, `name`.\n\nWhich types take children, which take named slots, which take neither:\n\n{{childrenTable}}\n\nA type with "no decoration" draws no box: put it inside a `box`, `row`, `column` or `stack` that has the fill or\nborder.\n\n<a id="base-layout"></a>\n## Layout\n\n`layout` says how big a node is and where it sits in its parent. Every field: [layout fields](layout.md#layout-layout-fields).\n\n<a id="base-width-and-height"></a>\n### Width and height\n\nEach axis has a **mode** and a **number**:\n\n| JSON | Mode | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `120` | fixed | Exactly 120. |\n| `{"hug": 120}` | hug | The size of the content (a text\'s lines, a row\'s children plus padding). |\n| `{"fill": 120}` | fill | All the room the parent gives: the free space along a row\'s or column\'s main axis (shared by `flex`), the whole cross axis, the whole box of a stack or canvas slot. |\n| `{"flexible": 120}` | flexible | Up to 120, less if a row or column runs out of room (main axis only). |\n\nThe number is the **design size**: the size of a fixed node, and the size used where a mode cannot apply (a fill\ninside something that scrolls on that axis, or inside a parent that hugs that axis: `fill_fallback`). For `hug` and\n`fill` it does not limit the size: cap a fill with `"constraints": {"maxWidth": 760}`. **A node without `width` or\n`height` is 0 × 0 and draws nothing** (`zero_size`); give every node both, except a `canvas` and a `spacer`.\n\n<a id="base-rows-columns-and-flex"></a>\n### Rows, columns and flex\n\n`row` and `column` lay their children along their **main axis**; `flex` is the same with a `direction`\n(`horizontal` | `vertical`) a media rule can change. Props: `mainAxisAlignment` (default `start`;\n`spaceBetween`...), `crossAxisAlignment` (default **`center`**: write `start` for left-aligned content, `stretch` to\nfill), `spacing` (the gap), `wrap` (flow onto new lines, like `Wrap`; `runSpacing` between lines). A child of a row\nor column may set in its own `layout`:\n\n- `flex`: its share of the free space when its main-axis size is `fill` or `flexible` (default 1);\n- `align`: its alignment in its slot, `[x, y]` from -1 to 1 or a name (`"centerRight"`);\n- `order` (CSS `order`): children are laid out by ascending order, equal orders as listed;\n- `basis` (CSS `flex-basis`, in a **wrapping** row): the size the child counts when lines break; with a `fill`\n  main size it then grows by its `flex` share of its line. `"width": {"fill": 300}, "basis": 280` is CSS\n  `flex: 1 1 280px`: three across at 1000 px, two at 700, one at 390.\n\nA child hidden by a binding or a media rule takes no room (CSS `display: none`). A `spacer` takes the free space\nonly in a row or column that has some (a fill or fixed main size).\n\n<a id="base-padding-margin-constraints-a-capped-width"></a>\n### Padding, margin, constraints, a capped width\n\n- `padding` is space inside the node\'s box, `margin` outside it: a number (all sides) or **four** numbers\n  `[left, top, right, bottom]` (two numbers are not read).\n- `constraints`: `{"minWidth", "maxWidth", "minHeight", "maxHeight"}`. `aspectRatio`: width / height.\n- **A full-width band with capped, centered content** (CSS `max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto`): the band fills\n  the width and holds the background; its one child fills with `"constraints": {"maxWidth": 1200}`, centered by the\n  band\'s `crossAxisAlignment` (`center`, the default). [The capped band, with an example](layout.md#layout-a-capped-band).\n- A negative margin does not overlap a neighbour: to overlap, move what the node paints with `"motion":\n  {"translateY": -36}` (layout unchanged), or use a stack. [Overlap and bleed](layout.md#layout-overlap-and-bleed).\n\n<a id="base-stacks"></a>\n### Stacks\n\nA `stack` places each child by its `layout.x` and `layout.y`: `16` or `{"start": 16}` from the left/top,\n`{"end": 16}` from the right/bottom, `{"start": 16, "end": 16}` stretched between, `{"align": 0}` aligned (-1 start,\n0 center, 1 end). Later children paint on top. `x`/`y` mean nothing under a row or column, `flex`/`align` nothing\nunder a stack (`layout_field_ignored`).\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["board"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "board": {"type": "canvas", "slots": {"body": "stage"}, "layout": {"width": 400, "height": 300}},\n    "stage": {\n      "type": "stack",\n      "children": ["photo", "badge", "caption"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 400}, "height": {"fill": 300}},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFE5E7EB"}]}\n    },\n    "photo": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 200, "height": 120, "x": {"align": 0}, "y": {"align": 0}},\n      "decoration": {\n        "fills": [\n          {\n            "type": "linear",\n            "stops": [{"position": 0, "color": "#FF6366F1"}, {"position": 1, "color": "#FFEC4899"}]\n          }\n        ],\n        "radius": 16\n      }\n    },\n    "badge": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 48, "height": 48, "x": {"end": 16}, "y": {"start": 16}},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF59E0B"}], "shape": "circle"}\n    },\n    "caption": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 100}, "height": {"hug": 20}, "x": {"start": 16, "end": 16}, "y": {"end": 16}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "Pinned 16 px from the left, right and bottom",\n        "textAlign": "center",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF374151"}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<a id="base-decoration"></a>\n## Decoration\n\n`decoration` paints the node\'s box:\n\n- `fills`: paints, bottom to top. `{"color": "#FF2563EB"}` is solid; a gradient is `{"type": "linear", "stops":\n  [{"position": 0, "color": ...}, {"position": 1, "color": ...}]}` (`"begin"`/`"end"` alignments; also `radial`,\n  `sweep`); an image is `{"type": "image", "image": {"url": "...", "fit": "cover"}}` (give the box the image\'s size\n  or an `aspectRatio`).\n- `strokes` with `strokeWidth` (default 1): the border. `radius`: a number or `[topLeft, topRight, bottomRight,\n  bottomLeft]`. `shape: "circle"`.\n- `effects`: `{"type": "dropShadow", "color": "#1F000000", "offset": [0, 4], "blurRadius": 12}`; an effect needs\n  its `type`.\n- `clip: "antiAlias"` clips the children to the rounded box.\n\nColours are `"#AARRGGBB"` (alpha first: `#FF` opaque, `#80` half), `"#RRGGBB"` or a theme colour\'s name; `"#FFF"`,\n`rgb()` and CSS names are not read. Patterns in pixels, grain, foreground scrims, icons, paths and custom drawing:\n[decoration](decoration.md#page-decoration).\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["deco"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "deco": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "row"},\n      "layout": {"width": 520, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF9FAFB"}]}\n    },\n    "row": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["card", "gradient", "outlined"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 520}, "height": {"fill": 200}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 24, "mainAxisAlignment": "center"}\n    },\n    "card": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {\n        "fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}],\n        "radius": 12,\n        "effects": [{"type": "dropShadow", "color": "#33000000", "offset": [0, 4], "blurRadius": 16}]\n      }\n    },\n    "gradient": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {\n        "fills": [\n          {\n            "type": "radial",\n            "stops": [{"position": 0, "color": "#FFFDE68A"}, {"position": 1, "color": "#FFF97316"}]\n          }\n        ],\n        "radius": [24, 4, 24, 4]\n      }\n    },\n    "outlined": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {"strokes": [{"color": "#FF2563EB"}], "strokeWidth": 2, "dashPattern": [6, 4], "radius": 12}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<a id="base-text"></a>\n## Text\n\nA `text` node has `props.text` and `props.style`: a theme style\'s name (`"style": "body"`) or a TextStyle\n(`fontSize`, `fontWeight` 100–900, `fontFamily`, `color`, `height` as a multiple of the size, `letterSpacing`,\n`decoration`, `fontStyle`), plus `textAlign`, `maxLines` and `overflow` (`ellipsis`).\n\n- **No `color`: the text is painted white.** Always set it (in the style or the named style).\n- No `fontSize`: 12. No `fontWeight`: 400. No `fontFamily`: the platform\'s default (Roboto). No `height`: the\n  nearest `defaultTextStyle`\'s, else the font\'s own line height ([text](theme.md#theme-text)).\n- Size: one line `{"hug": n}` × `{"hug": n}`; a paragraph `{"fill": n}` wide (it wraps) × `{"hug": n}` high.\n- `text` may hold expressions: `"Hello, \${user.name}"`; `"\$\${price}"` shows `\$47`.\n- Symbols the font has no glyph for (✦, ✓, →) draw as empty boxes (`missing_glyph`): use an `icon` node.\n\nRuns (parts in another style), superscripts, links in text: [text](theme.md#theme-text).\n\n<a id="base-the-base-node-types"></a>\n## The base node types\n\nThe props that matter most; each type\'s page lists all of them.\n\n{{baseTypes}}\n\n- **Buttons**: the text is `label` (not `text`); colours, corners and the label\'s style are in `style` (a\n  [ButtonStyle](forms.md#type-ButtonStyle): `backgroundColor`, `foregroundColor`, `textStyle`, `shape`), not in\n  `decoration`. Give a button a fixed width or a fill: a hugging button is only as wide as its label. For full\n  control, use a `row` with a fill, padding, a text child and a `click` reaction.\n- **Inputs** (`textField`, `checkbox`, `switch`, `radio`, `slider`, `dropdown`, `segmentedButton`) report a new\n  value through their `changed` trigger as `\${result}`: store it with `setVariable`. **Two-way**: bind the value\n  prop to the variable (`"bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${query}"}` for a text field, `"props.value"` for the\n  others). A text field\'s label, hint, border and fill are in `props.decoration` (an\n  [InputDecoration](forms.md#type-InputDecoration)). Styling every control, validation: [forms](forms.md#page-forms).\n- **Lists**: a `listView` or `gridView` repeats its **first child** once per item of its `data` binding:\n  `"bind": {"data": "\${plans}"}`; inside, `\${item.name}` and `\${index}`. An item fills the list across (its\n  cross-axis size is `fill`). In a page that scrolls, give the list\n  `"scrollable": false` (a gridView: `"physics": "never"`). A grid of as many equal columns as fit:\n  `minCrossAxisExtent` (CSS `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))`); equal-height cards: `"shrinkWrapRows": true`.\n  Nested lists, tables, pagination: [lists](lists.md#page-lists).\n- **Icons**: `props.icon` is a Material icon name (`"arrow_forward"`, `"check_circle"`; `_outlined`, `_rounded`\n  suffixes), with `color` and `size`.\n- **Images**: an image fill on a `box` (see Decoration). **Divider**: `divider` with `thickness` and `color`, or a\n  `box` 1 high with a fill.\n\n<a id="base-variables-bindings-and-expressions"></a>\n## Variables, bindings and expressions\n\n**Variables** hold state. Declare them in the document\'s `variables` under a canvas id (that screen) or\n`"page_variables"` (every canvas of the document):\n\n```json\n"variables": {"page_variables": [\n  {"name": "annual", "type": "boolean", "value": false},\n  {"name": "plans", "type": "list", "value": [{"name": "Team", "monthly": 39}]},\n  {"name": "price", "type": "number", "formula": "annual ? plans[0].monthly * 0.8 : plans[0].monthly"},\n  {"name": "usd", "type": "text", "parameters": ["n"], "formula": "\'\$\' + round(n)"}\n]}\n```\n\nTypes: {{variableTypes}}. A variable with a `formula` is **computed**: read-only, it follows what it reads. With\n`parameters` it is a **function** any formula calls (`\${= usd(price * 12)}`). Write a rule once, not in every\nbinding.\n\n**Expressions**: `\${name}` or `\${path}` reads a value (`\${user.name}`, `\${items[0].price}`, `\${item.title}`);\n`\${= formula}` computes one (`\${= count * price}`, `\${= annual ? \'Yearly\' : \'Monthly\'}`, a list\n`\${= popular ? [0, 0, 0, 0] : [0, 28, 0, 0]}`). A text that is exactly one expression keeps the value\'s type. `\${false}` reads a variable called `false`: a literal is `\${= false}`.\nEvery formula function, grouped (text, numbers, money, lists, dates): [formula functions](state.md#state-formula-functions).\n\n**Bindings** put an expression on a field: `"bind": {path: expression}`, updated whenever what it reads changes.\n\n```json\n"bind": {"props.text": "\${= \'Total: \' + money(count * price, \'\$\')}", "visible": "\${= count > 0}",\n         "decoration.fills[0].color": "\${= selected ? \'#FFDBEAFE\' : \'#FFFFFFFF\'}"}\n```\n\nPaths: `visible`, `opacity`, `layout.<field>`, `decoration.<field>` (`fills[0].color`), `props.<prop>` and\n`props.<prop>.<field>`, `data`, `selected`, `disabled`, behavior keys. Other fields are literal: `"opacity":\n"\${x}"` is an error; bind it. What each path expects: [binding paths](state.md#state-binding-paths).\n\n<a id="base-reactions"></a>\n## Reactions\n\nA node\'s `actions` is a list of **reactions**: a trigger and the actions it runs, in order:\n\n```json\n"actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"},\n             "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "count", "op": "add", "value": "1"},\n                         {"type": "navigate", "to": "thanks"}]}]\n```\n\n- Triggers: `click`, `hover`, `changed` (an input\'s value), `submitted`, `load` (on a canvas), `valueChanged`,\n  `timer`... (all of them: [triggers](interaction.md#interaction-triggers)).\n- `setVariable` (`op`: `set` (default), `toggle`, `add`, `subtract`, `insert`, `removeAt`...; `value` is an\n  expression), `navigate` (`to`: a canvas id; `"mode": "pop"` goes back), `openModal` / `closeModal`, `showToast`,\n  `if` (`"condition"`: a predicate, `{"left": "\${count}", "op": "greaterThan", "right": "5"}` or `{"left":\n  "\${= valid}", "op": "isTrue"}`; `then` and `else`: action lists), `scrollTo`, `componentEvent` (a component\'s event, or at run time the event\n  to the host app). Action types here: {{actionTypes}}.\n- Keys are exact; validation names the one meant: `{"type": "scrollTo", "node": "faq"}`, `{"type":\n  "copyToClipboard", "text": "\${address}"}`, `{"type": "downloadFile", "fileName": "trip.txt", "text": "\${brief}"}`;\n  a list appends with `"op": "add"` (`insert` takes an `index`).\n- In a chain `\${result}` is the trigger\'s event (a text field\'s text) until an action gives another value.\n- A tap on a control inside a tappable row runs the control\'s reaction only: to toggle from the whole row, give the\n  control `"ignorePointer": true` and bind its value.\n\nHover and pressed styles (`states`), drag, gestures: [interaction](interaction.md#page-interaction). Screens and modals:\n[navigation](navigation.md#page-navigation).\n\n<a id="base-screen-sizes-media-rules"></a>\n## Screen sizes: media rules\n\n1. Prefer layout that fits any width: wrapping rows with `basis`, a `gridView` with `minCrossAxisExtent`, a capped\n   band.\n2. A node\'s `media` is a list of CSS media queries over the node: `[{"minWidth": 600, "patch": {"props": {"style":\n   {"fontSize": 40}}}}]`. `minWidth`/`maxWidth` are px (inclusive) or a breakpoint name (`"tablet"`).\n3. The `patch` is shaped like the node (`props`, `layout`, `decoration`, `visible`, `motion`, `bind`) and merged\n   over it; later rules win (the cascade). Write for phones, add `minWidth` rules (mobile first).\n4. A row that becomes a column: a `flex` with a rule patching `"direction": "vertical"`; another order: patch\n   `layout.order`; hidden: `"visible": false`.\n5. A field both patched and bound shows the binding (`media_overridden`): put the binding in the rule\'s patch.\n\nBreakpoints, sticky headers, scrolling, a canvas per breakpoint: [responsive layout](layout.md#page-layout).\n\n<a id="base-rules-that-are-easy-to-get-wrong"></a>\n## Rules that are easy to get wrong\n\n1. Every node needs `layout.width` and `layout.height`; without them it is 0 × 0.\n2. Every text needs a colour; without one it is white.\n3. Padding and margin are a number or four numbers, never two.\n4. Colours are `#AARRGGBB`, `#RRGGBB` or a theme colour\'s name; define the theme first and name its colours and\n   styles.\n5. Columns center their children across by default: `"crossAxisAlignment": "start"` for left-aligned content.\n6. A screen taller than the window needs a scrolling body column (`"scrollable": true`, `fill` both ways).\n7. Values in `props`, `layout` and `decoration` are literal; expressions go in `bind` (except `props.text`).\n8. `x`/`y` only work under a `stack`; `flex`/`align` only under a `row`, `column` or `flex`.\n9. Ids are map keys; a child is listed in exactly one parent; canvases are only in `roots`.\n10. `fill` takes all the room it is given: cap it with `constraints.maxWidth`. Under a parent that hugs that\n    axis, a fill is its design number (`fill_fallback`).\n11. A backslash in a formula is written twice in JSON: `"\${= matches(code, \'^\\\\d{4}\$\')}"`.\n12. Buttons: `label`, colours in `style`. Inputs: `changed` + `setVariable`, two-way by binding the value prop.\n13. Repeated content comes from data: one template in a `listView` / `gridView`, not copies.\n\n'),
  BaseSegment(['files'], '<a id="base-checking-your-work"></a>\n## Checking your work\n\nDecoding is lenient: a misspelled key or a value of the wrong shape is silently dropped. Never trust a document\nthat has not been checked. Run the render command from the SDK repository:\n\n```sh\ntool/render/render.sh site/ --out shots/ --sizes 390x844,834x1112,1440x900 --full-page\n```\n\nIt validates every document strictly, renders each screen at each size (`shots/<screen>@<w>x<h>.png`,\n`shots/diagnostics.json`) and prints one line per problem: a code, the JSON pointer\n(`/nodes/hero-title/props/style/fontSize`) and what to do. It exits 1 on errors. Steps before the capture:\n`--tap <id>` (`<id>#<n>` for the n-th list item), `--hover`, `--focus`, `--type <id>=<text>`,\n`--set <variable>=<json>`, `--scroll <id>=<px>`, `--drag <id>=<dx>,<dy>`, `--navigate <canvas>?<param>=<value>`,\n`--label <name>`. Look at the\nscreenshots: validation cannot tell you a page is ugly. Every option and diagnostic code: [render](render.md#page-render).\n\n<a id="base-sites-and-components-as-files"></a>\n## Sites and components as files\n\nA page longer than a screen or two is easier to write, fix and reuse as parts, each a file: a **component** is a\ndocument with one root and a `widget` declaration of its parameters, slots and events, read inside as\n`\${props.price}`; a page **calls** it with one node of that type (`{"type": "PlanCard", "props": {"price": 47}}`),\nas Flutter builds `PlanCard(price: 47)`. A component never reads its page\'s variables: pass what it needs as\nparameters, and shared state as a `variable` parameter. A folder with `site.json` (pages, components, theme,\nproject variables) is a site. **Write `site.json` first, with every page listed in `pages`**, before the pages\nthat link to them: a link to a page not listed yet is an `unknown_screen` error.\n\n- **List template**: one shape repeated from data in one parent.\n- **Component**: the same structure in two or more places with different values (a card, a chip).\n- **Section**: a top-level band of a page (header, hero, pricing, FAQ, footer), in its own file when it is more\n  than about 15 nodes.\n\nParameter kinds, slots, events, the manifest, rendering one part: [components](components.md#page-components). A whole site\n(manifest, shared header and footer, route parameters, storage, a modal): [a complete site](components.md#components-a-complete-multi-page-site).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n'),
  BaseSegment(['runtime'], '<a id="base-ops"></a>\n## Ops\n\n`{"ops": [op, ...]}`, applied in order:\n\n{{ops}}\n\n<a id="base-examples"></a>\n## Examples\n\nBuild (a card with a selectable list and a labelled button):\n\n{{buildExample}}\n\nChange it ("make it say Lisbon and add a note"):\n\n{{editExample}}\n\nEvery op rule, streaming and the retry protocol: [edit ops](edit-ops.md#page-edit-ops).\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n'),
  BaseSegment(['index'], '<a id="base-index"></a>\n## Index\n\n{{index}}\n'),
  BaseSegment([], '\n'),
];

/// The reference's pages by section: what `ui_docs` serves (`docs/reference/<id>.md`).
const List<DocPage> docPages = [
  DocPage(
    id: 'layout',
    title: 'Responsive layout',
    summary: 'Sizes, rows and columns, stacks, scrolling and screen sizes beyond the base: every layout field, which sizing modes each parent allows, media rules and breakpoints, and the web layouts agents ask for (a capped band, cards that wrap, a row that becomes a column, overlap and bleed, a sticky header or column).',
    when: 'Sizes, rows and columns, stacks, scrolling and screen sizes beyond the base: every layout field, which sizing\nmodes each parent allows, media rules and breakpoints, and the web layouts agents ask for (a capped band, cards that\nwrap, a row that becomes a column, overlap and bleed, a sticky header or column).',
    example: 'The text hugs its content, the red box fills the column\'s width, and in the row the green and blue boxes share the\nfree space 1 : 2 (`flex`) beside a fixed grey box.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["sizing"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "sizing": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 400, "height": 400},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["hugText", "fillBox", "bar"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 400}, "height": {"fill": 400}, "padding": 10},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 8}\n    },\n    "hugText": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 80}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "As wide as its text", "style": {"fontSize": 16, "color": "#FF000000"}}\n    },\n    "fillBox": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 380}, "height": 24},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFEF4444"}]}\n    },\n    "bar": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["one", "two", "fixed"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 380}, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"spacing": 10}\n    },\n    "one": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 100}, "height": {"fill": 40}},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF22C55E"}]}\n    },\n    "two": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 200}, "height": {"fill": 40}, "flex": 2},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF3B82F6"}]}\n    },\n    "fixed": {"type": "box", "layout": {"width": 60, "height": 20}, "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF9CA3AF"}]}}\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- `fill` takes all the room it is given: cap it with `constraints.maxWidth`. Where its parent gives no room on that\n  axis (it hugs it, or scrolls), a fill is its design number (`fill_fallback`, naming the parent).\n- `x`/`y` mean nothing under a row or column, `flex`/`align` nothing under a stack (`layout_field_ignored`).\n- A stack that hugs its children grows to hold them, so there a negative offset is 0 (`layout_clamped`). A\n  negative margin does not overlap a neighbour (`layout_clamped`): translate with `motion`.\n- A media patch replaces a size of another mode: `{"hug": 200}` over `{"fill": 292}` is `{"hug": 200}`. A field\n  both patched and bound shows the binding (`media_overridden`): bind in the rule instead.\n- `squeezeChildren` (default true) shrinks children that do not fit toward their content, as CSS flex items\n  shrink; false is Flutter\'s overflow (`layout_overflow`).\n- A `spacer` takes the free space only in a row or column with room to spare.\n- Without `basis`, children of a wrapping row keep their own size.\n- `\${screen.width}` prints a decimal (`390.0`); `\${= screen.width}` prints `390`.',
    words: 7037,
    items: ['canvas', 'row', 'column', 'flex', 'stack', 'box', 'spacer', 'divider', 'verticalDivider', 'variance', 'sticky', 'floating', 'measure', 'scroll', 'scrollEnd', 'enterViewport', 'exitViewport', 'scrollTo'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('layout-layout-fields', 'Layout fields', 'A node\'s `"layout"`: its size, spacing and placement in its parent. `width` and `height` are an\n[AxisSize](values.md#type-AxisSize): a number (fixed) or `{"fill" | "hug" | "flexible" | "fixed": number}`; `x` and `y` an\n[AxisPosition](values.md#type-AxisPosition).\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `width` | [AxisSize](values.md#type-AxisSize) | `0` |  | The node\'s width: a number (fixed), `{"hug": n}` (its content), `{"fill": n}` (the room its parent gives) or `{"flexible": n}` (up to n). n is the design size. Without one the node is 0 wide. |\n| `height` | [AxisSize](values.md#type-AxisSize) | `0` |  | The node\'s height: a number (fixed), `{"hug": n}`, `{"fill": n}` or `{"flexible": n}`, as `width`. Without one the node is 0 high. |\n| `constraints` | [BoxConstraints](values.md#type-BoxConstraints) | `{}` |  |  |\n| `margin` | [EdgeInsets](values.md#type-EdgeInsets) | `0` |  | Space around the node, outside its box. |\n| `padding` | [EdgeInsets](values.md#type-EdgeInsets) | `0` |  | Space between the node\'s box and its content (Flutter\'s `Padding`). A text\'s padding sits around its lines, as `Padding(child: Text(...))`: a hugging text grows by it (schema 3; schema 2 ignored it on a text, and the migration drops it there). |\n| `aspectRatio` | double | unset | ≥ 0 | Width / height the node keeps when its parent resizes it. |\n| `flex` | int | `1` | ≥ 0 | Under a row/column: share of the free space (`Expanded.flex`). |\n| `squeezable` | bool | `false` |  | Under a row/column: a hugging child that may shrink (`Flexible`). |\n| `x` | [AxisPosition](values.md#type-AxisPosition) | `{"start":0}` |  | Under a freeform parent (`Positioned` / `Align`). |\n| `y` | [AxisPosition](values.md#type-AxisPosition) | `{"start":0}` |  | Position under a freeform parent. |\n| `align` | [Alignment](values.md#type-Alignment) | unset |  | Under a row/column: alignment in its slot (`Align`). |\n| `order` | int | `0` |  | CSS `order`: under a row, column or flex, children are laid out and painted by ascending order (equal orders as listed). Patch it per screen size (`media`) to reorder at a width. |\n| `basis` | double | unset | ≥ 0 | CSS `flex-basis`, under a wrapping row, column or flex: the main size the child counts when lines are broken; a child that fills the main axis (`{"fill": n}`) then grows by its `flex` share of the room left on its line (`flex: 1 1 280px`). Cards with `basis: 280` sit three across at 900 px, two at 600, one at 390, with no breakpoints. |\n\nRead by decoding but not declared as fields: `widthFactor`, `heightFactor`. A share (0–1 and up) of the room its parent gives it on that axis (`FractionallySizedBox`): a progress bar\'s fill is `widthFactor: 0.6` of its track. Null: sized by `width` / `height`. Bindable (`layout.widthFactor`).'),
      DocSection('layout-which-sizing-modes-each-parent-allows', 'Which sizing modes each parent allows', 'From the parents\' own rules; "fill (with `basis`)": a child of a wrapping row may fill its line\'s share when it sets\n`layout.basis`.\n\n| Parent | Width may be | Height may be |\n|---|---|---|\n| `row` | fixed, fill, flexible, hug | fixed, fill, hug |\n| `column` | fixed, fill, hug | fixed, fill, flexible, hug |\n| `row` with {"wrap":true} | fixed, fill (with `basis`), hug | fixed, fill, hug |\n| `column` with {"scrollable":true} | fixed, fill, hug | fixed, hug |\n| `row` with {"scrollable":true,"scrollDirection":"horizontal"} | fixed, hug | fixed, fill, hug |\n| `stack` | fixed, fill, hug | fixed, fill, hug |\n| `canvas` | fixed, fill, hug | fixed, fill, hug |\n| `listView` | fill | fixed, hug |\n| `listView` with {"itemExtent":80} | fill | fill |\n| `gridView` | fill | fill |\n| `pageView` | fill | fill |\n\nWhy a mode is not allowed, as the declarations say it:\n\n- Flexible only applies in a row or column, along its main axis.\n- A wrapping row lays its children out in runs: they keep their own size along it, unless they set layout.basis (CSS flex-basis): then a filling child grows to share its line.\n- The column scrolls: its content has no end to fill to.\n- The row scrolls: its content has no end to fill to.\n- Items in a list always fill across it.\n- A list is unbounded along its scroll axis: items cannot fill it. Set an item extent.\n- The list gives every item its item extent: they fill it.\n- Grid cells size their children: they fill them.\n- Pages size their children: they fill them.'),
      DocSection('layout-media-rules', 'Media rules', 'A node\'s `media` (and the theme\'s) is a list of rules, each a CSS media query over the node:\n\n| Key | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `minWidth` | CSS `min-width`: a width in px (inclusive), or a breakpoint name (from its min width). |\n| `maxWidth` | CSS `max-width`: a width in px (inclusive), or a breakpoint name (up to the next breakpoint\'s min width, exclusive). |\n| `orientation` | CSS `orientation`. |\n| `patch` | A JSON merge patch over the node (maps merge, `null` removes, anything else replaces): `props`, `layout`, `decoration`, `visible`, `opacity`, `motion` (a transform that moves what is painted, not the layout: `Transform.translate`), and `bind`: bindings that hold at these sizes only (`"bind": {"visible": "\${= !open}"}`), or `null` to drop one of the node\'s own here, so its patched value shows. |'),
      DocSection('layout-breakpoints', 'Breakpoints', 'The project\'s breakpoints name size classes by minimum width. Unless a document\'s `breakpoints` key says otherwise\nthey are:\n\n| id | name | minWidth | design width × height |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `mobile` | Mobile | 0 | 390 × 844 |\n| `tablet` | Tablet | 600 | 834 × 1112 |\n| `desktop` | Desktop | 1024 | 1440 × 900 |\n\nA breakpoint\'s fields:\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `id` | String | `""` |  | Stable id. |\n| `name` | String | `""` |  | Name. |\n| `minWidth` | double | `0` | ≥ 0 | From this width (inclusive). |\n| `width` | double | `0` | ≥ 0 | Design width of its canvases. |\n| `height` | double | `0` | ≥ 0 | Design height of its canvases. |'),
      DocSection('layout-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-scroll"></a>`scroll` | The node (a scrolling row, column or canvas) scrolled (`\${result.offset}`, `\${result.max}`, `\${result.fraction}`), or came near its end (load the next page). |\n| <a id="trigger-scrollEnd"></a>`scrollEnd` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-enterViewport"></a>`enterViewport` | At least `Trigger.visibleFraction` of the node became visible (and stayed so for `Trigger.visibleMs`), or it fell below that after being visible. With `Trigger.onceKey` (`\${item.id}`), an impression: once per item per app session. |\n| <a id="trigger-exitViewport"></a>`exitViewport` |  |'),
      DocSection('layout-responsive-design', 'Responsive design', 'Responsive layout works as on the web: flexbox and grid lay content out so it fits any width, and media queries\nchange what must change at a width. Use these, in this order:\n\n1. **Intrinsic layout, no breakpoints.** A wrapping row whose children set `layout.basis` and fill the main axis:\n   lines break by the basis and the children on each line grow to share it. For repeated data, a `gridView` with\n   `minCrossAxisExtent` makes as many equal columns as fit. A share of the parent (CSS `width: 60%`) is\n   `layout.widthFactor: 0.6`.\n2. **Media rules** for what must change at a width: direction, order, visibility, type size, padding. A rule\'s\n   `patch` is merged over the node (objects merge, `null` removes a key), except that a value with several forms is\n   **replaced**, as CSS replaces a declaration: `{"width": {"hug": 200}}` over `{"fill": 292}` is `{"hug": 200}`.\n   Rules apply in order, a later one winning (the cascade). Validation checks every patched value and judges sizes\n   at each range of widths with the rules that hold there.\n3. **Bindings on `\${screen}`** for values computed from the size: `"bind": {"layout.width": "\${= min(screen.width -\n   32, 760)}"}`. `\${screen}` has `width`, `height`, `breakpoint`, `is.<name>`, `atLeast.<name>`\n   (`\${= screen.atLeast.tablet ? 3 : 1}`). Nothing can check such a formula\'s result: prefer media rules.\n4. **A canvas per breakpoint**, only for screens that are genuinely different designs (below).\n\nPrecedence: the node\'s own values, then its media rules, then an active interaction state\'s patch, then its\nbindings, then conditions.\n\nThis page uses the four web patterns: a header whose links collapse to a menu icon below desktop, a 3 → 2 → 1 card\ngrid from data (`minCrossAxisExtent`), a text-and-photo section that stacks with the photo first on phones (`basis`\nin a wrapping row, the photo\'s `order` patched), and a title whose size steps up with the width, inside a content\ncolumn capped at 1200:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 1440, "height": 900},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["header", "content"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1440}, "height": {"fill": 900}},\n      "props": {"scrollable": true}\n    },\n    "header": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["logo", "nav", "menu"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1440}, "height": 64, "padding": [16, 0, 16, 0]},\n      "props": {"mainAxisAlignment": "spaceBetween"},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF111827"}]},\n      "media": [{"minWidth": "desktop", "patch": {"layout": {"padding": [32, 0, 32, 0]}}}]\n    },\n    "logo": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 80}, "height": {"hug": 24}},\n      "props": {"text": "Relay", "style": {"fontSize": 20, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FFFFFFFF"}}\n    },\n    "nav": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["nav-1", "nav-2", "nav-3"],\n      "visible": false,\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 300}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"spacing": 32},\n\n(Continues: layout.md#layout-responsive-design.)'),
      DocSection('layout-a-capped-band', 'A capped band', 'A full-width band with capped, centered content (CSS `max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto` inside a coloured band):\nthe band fills the width and holds the background; its one child fills with `constraints.maxWidth`, centered by the\nband\'s `crossAxisAlignment` (`center`, the default). Under `crossAxisAlignment: stretch` a cap holds too, as CSS\n`max-width` does: the child sits at the start, or where its `layout.align` puts it (`[0, 0]` centers it). Below, a\ncomparison table built from one row template and one cell template:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 1440, "height": 900},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["band"],\n      "props": {"scrollable": true},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1440}, "height": {"fill": 900}}\n    },\n    "band": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["rail"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1440}, "height": {"hug": 200}, "padding": [24, 48, 24, 48]},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF1F2937"}]}\n    },\n    "rail": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["title", "table"],\n      "props": {"spacing": 16, "crossAxisAlignment": "stretch"},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1200}, "height": {"hug": 160}, "constraints": {"maxWidth": 1200}}\n    },\n    "title": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "props": {"text": "Compare plans", "style": {"fontSize": 28, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1200}, "height": {"hug": 34}}\n    },\n    "table": {\n      "type": "listView",\n      "children": ["tr"],\n      "bind": {"data": "\${rows}"},\n      "props": {"physics": "never"},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1200}, "height": {"hug": 120}}\n    },\n    "tr": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["label", "cells"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1200}, "height": {"hug": 44}},\n      "decoration": {"strokes": [{"color": "#FF374151"}], "strokeSides": "bottom"}\n    },\n    "label": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "bind": {"props.text": "\${item.label}"},\n      "props": {"text": "", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FFD1D5DB"}},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 180}, "height": {"hug": 20}, "flex": 2}\n    },\n    "cells": {\n      "type": "gridView",\n      "children": ["cell"],\n      "bind": {"data": "\${item.values}", "props.crossAxisCount": "\${= length(item.values)}"},\n      "props": {"physics": "never", "crossAxisCount": 3, "shrinkWrapRows": true},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 600}, "height": {"hug": 44}, "flex": 3}\n    },\n    "cell": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "bind": {"props.text": "\${item}"},\n      "props": {"text": "", "textAlign": "center", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 200}, "height": {"hug": 20}, "margin": [0, 12, 0, 12]}\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "home": [\n      {\n        "name": "rows",\n        "type": "list",\n        "value": [\n          {"label": "Seats", "values": ["5", "25", "Unlimited"]},\n          {"label": "SSO", "values": ["–", "Yes", "Yes"]},\n\n(Continues: layout.md#layout-a-capped-band.)'),
      DocSection('layout-cards-that-wrap', 'Cards that wrap', 'Three plan cards three across at desktop, two at tablet, one on phones, with no breakpoint: a wrapping `row`\n(`"wrap": true`, `spacing`, `runSpacing`) whose cards are `"width": {"fill": 300}, "basis": 280`. With\n`crossAxisAlignment: stretch` the cards of each line are as tall as its tallest (CSS `align-items: stretch`: equal\nheights). From data, use a `gridView` with `minCrossAxisExtent` and `shrinkWrapRows` instead\n([equal-height cards](lists.md#lists-equal-height-cards)).'),
      DocSection('layout-a-row-that-becomes-a-column', 'A row that becomes a column', 'A `flex` node with `"direction": "horizontal"` and a rule patching `"direction": "vertical"` below a width. Its\nchildren stay the same nodes, keeping their state. Another order at a width: each child\'s `layout.order`, patched in\nthe child\'s own rule (`{"maxWidth": "mobile", "patch": {"layout": {"order": -1}}}` puts it first). Hidden at a\nwidth: `{"maxWidth": "tablet", "patch": {"visible": false}}`; a hidden node takes no room.\n\n```json\n"split": {"type": "flex", "children": ["copy", "photo"], "props": {"direction": "horizontal", "spacing": 32},\n          "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1200}, "height": {"hug": 400}},\n          "media": [{"maxWidth": 599, "patch": {"props": {"direction": "vertical"}}}]}\n```'),
      DocSection('layout-a-media-rule-and-a-binding-on-one-field', 'A media rule and a binding on one field', 'Shown on phones only, and there only while a panel is closed: a patch may set `bind`, bindings that hold at its\nsizes only. Write the node for the other sizes and bind in the rule: `"visible": false, "media": [{"maxWidth": 599,\n"patch": {"bind": {"visible": "\${= !filtersOpen}"}}}]`. The breakpoint stays in the media rule. To show a patched\nvalue where the node binds the field at other sizes, drop the binding in the rule: `"patch": {"visible": true,\n"bind": {"visible": null}}`.'),
      DocSection('layout-overlap-and-bleed', 'Overlap and bleed', '**Overlapping a neighbour** (CSS `margin-top: -36px`, `transform: translateY(-36px)`): Flutter\'s answer is\n`Transform.translate`: `"motion": {"translateY": -36}` moves what the node paints, not its layout, so the next node\ndoes not move up; a node later in its parent paints over the ones before it. A media rule may patch it. A card\noverlapping the bottom of a hero band: the card after the hero with `translateY: -36`, and 36 px of `margin` below it\nif the next section should keep its distance. The render command reports a node translated past its parent\'s box as\n`layout_overflow` (a warning naming the parent): expected for this pattern, and the only diagnostic it leaves. To\noverlap by an amount that depends on the content, or with no warning, use a `stack`.\n\n**Bleeding past the gutter** (a table or photo running to the screen\'s edge while the text keeps its padding): put\nthe padding on the children, not on the band, or let the one child that bleeds translate out of it (`"motion":\n{"translateX": 18}` with a width 18 larger), and keep the band\'s `"decoration": {"clip": "none"}` (the default). A\nphoto frame that overhangs its photo: a `stack` with a fixed or fill size holding the frame at a negative `x`/`y`.'),
      DocSection('layout-scrolling', 'Scrolling', 'A screen scrolls only if something in it scrolls. Make the canvas\'s body column scroll: `"props": {"scrollable":\ntrue}` with `{"fill": n}` width and height. Without it, content past the bottom of the screen is cut off\n(`offscreen`). Inside a scrolling column, a child cannot `fill` the scrolling axis. Rows scroll sideways with\n`"scrollable": true, "scrollDirection": "horizontal"`. `scrollTo` reveals a node (`"node"`: an id, or an expression\ngiving one; `"axis": "horizontal"` moves only sideways scroll views): `{"type": "scrollTo", "node": "faq",\n"durationMs": 400}` from a sub-navigation link (the key is `node`, not `target`).\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["article"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "article": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "scroller"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "scroller": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["header", "p1", "p2", "p3"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"scrollable": true, "spacing": 16, "crossAxisAlignment": "start"}\n    },\n    "header": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 400},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFDBEAFE"}], "radius": 16}\n    },\n    "p1": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 300},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFDE68A"}], "radius": 16}\n    },\n    "p2": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 300},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFBBF7D0"}], "radius": 16}\n    },\n    "p3": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "The end of the page.", "style": {"fontSize": 16, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```'),
      DocSection('layout-scroll-progress', 'Scroll progress', 'A reading-progress bar on an article or a long page: a `scroll` reaction on the page\'s scrolling column writes\n`\${result.fraction}` (0 at the top, 1 at the end) to a variable, and a `progressBar` (or a box\'s width factor) is\nbound to it. Put the bar outside the scrolling column (a `stack` over it, or the canvas\'s `appBar`) so it stays in\nview:\n\n```json\n"actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "scroll"},\n             "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "readFraction", "value": "\${result.fraction}"}]}]\n```\n\nand on the bar `"bind": {"props.value": "\${readFraction}"}`. Per section instead of per page: `viewProgress` on the\nsection ([view progress](animation.md#animation-reveal-on-scroll-view-progress-sticky-effects)).'),
      DocSection('layout-a-sticky-header-or-column', 'A sticky header or column', 'A header that stays at the top while the page scrolls under it: the scrolling column\'s first child with\n`"sticky": {"offset": 0}` (CSS `position: sticky`); it is drawn above the content and is pushed on by the end of\nits parent. `\${sticky.stuck}` is true while it is pinned (bind a shadow or a smaller height to it). A `--full-page`\ncapture draws it once, in its place in the page, as a reader sees it at the top; to see it pinned, capture a window\nscrolled down (`--scroll <scrolling column id>=1200` without `--full-page`). A header fixed to the window instead (it never\nscrolls, and a full-page capture draws it once, at the top): a `stack` filling the canvas body, the scrolling column\nfirst (with a top spacer of the header\'s height) and the header after it at `"y": 0`.\n\nA comparison table with a **sticky first column** on phones is two parts side by side: a fixed column of row\nlabels, and a row of plan columns that scrolls sideways (made to scroll only on phones by a media rule on its\n`scrollable`); give each table row the same height in both. From data: [a table from one template](lists.md#lists-a-table-from-one-template).'),
      DocSection('layout-a-canvas-per-breakpoint', 'A canvas per breakpoint', 'Canvases with the same `props.screen` are one screen; each sets `props.breakpoint` to the breakpoint it is for. At\na given width the screen shows the canvas whose breakpoint\'s `minWidth` is the highest at or below the width, else\nits narrowest. Each canvas has its own nodes; share state with `page_variables`. A `variance` node does the same for\none part of a screen. Older documents use this:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home-mobile", "home-desktop"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home-mobile": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "Home",\n      "props": {"screen": "home", "breakpoint": "mobile"},\n      "slots": {"body": "m-page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "m-page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["m-title", "m-size"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 8}\n    },\n    "m-title": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 32}},\n      "props": {"text": "Stacked for phones", "style": {"fontSize": 24, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "m-size": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "\${screen.breakpoint}: \${screen.width} px wide",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF6B7280"}\n      }\n    },\n    "home-desktop": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "Home",\n      "props": {"screen": "home", "breakpoint": "desktop"},\n      "slots": {"body": "d-page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 1440, "height": 900},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF3F4F6"}]}\n    },\n    "d-page": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["d-title", "d-size"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 1440}, "height": {"hug": 120}, "padding": 48},\n      "props": {"mainAxisAlignment": "spaceBetween"}\n    },\n    "d-title": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 400}, "height": {"hug": 48}},\n      "props": {"text": "Side by side on desktops", "style": {"fontSize": 40, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "d-size": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 200}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "\${screen.breakpoint}: \${screen.width} px wide",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF6B7280"}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["page"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "page": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["features"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24}\n    },\n    "features": {\n      "type": "variance",\n      "children": ["stacked", "sideBySide"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 200}},\n      "props": {\n        "variants": [\n          {"id": "narrow", "name": "Narrow", "breakpoint": "mobile", "children": ["stacked"]},\n\n(Continues: layout.md#layout-a-canvas-per-breakpoint.)'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'theme',
    title: 'Theme and text',
    summary: 'A site\'s palette and type scale, declared once and named everywhere; dark mode and a type scale that changes with the screen size; and the `text` node in depth (runs, links, superscripts, fonts, text direction).',
    when: 'A site\'s palette and type scale, declared once and named everywhere; dark mode and a type scale that changes with\nthe screen size; and the `text` node in depth (runs, links, superscripts, fonts, text direction).',
    example: 'A site manifest (`site.json`) with a theme: a palette and a type scale. The page next to it names them.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "pages": ["home.json"],\n  "theme": {\n    "colors": {"ink": "#FF1B1B1B", "ember": "#FFE4572E", "paper": "#FFF6F1E9"},\n    "textStyles": {\n      "body": {"fontSize": 16, "height": 1.5, "color": "ink"},\n      "title": {"from": "body", "fontSize": 32, "fontWeight": 700, "height": 1.2},\n      "eyebrow": {"from": "body", "fontSize": 12, "letterSpacing": 2, "color": "ember"}\n    },\n    "media": [{"minWidth": 1024, "patch": {"textStyles": {"title": {"fontSize": 56}}}}]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nA page using it (a fragment of `home.json`\'s `nodes`):\n\n```json\n"eyebrow": {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "OUR MENU", "style": "eyebrow"}, "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 18}}},\n"title":   {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "Fire, smoke and season", "style": "title"}, "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 40}}},\n"note":    {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "Cooked over oak.", "style": {"from": "body", "color": "ember"}}, "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 24}}},\n"rule":    {"type": "box", "layout": {"width": 120, "height": 4}, "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "ember"}]}}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- A text without a colour is white (`text_no_color` when rendered): set it in the style or the named style.\n- A name the theme does not have is `unknown_theme_name` (with the nearest name); a theme of the wrong shape is\n  `invalid_theme`. Without a `site.json`, put the page in a folder with one: `{"schema": 3, "pages": ["home.json"],\n  "theme": {...}}`.\n- A theme colour\'s name is not read from a formula: bind `\${theme.colors.ember}`.\n- Run offsets count characters, `\\n` as one.',
    words: 2632,
    items: ['text', 'textDirection', 'defaultTextStyle', 'setThemeMode'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('theme-theme-keys', 'Theme keys', 'The theme (`site.json`\'s `theme`, or the app\'s theme at run time):\n\n| Key | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `colors` | Every named color of the project by key (`themeKey` of its name: "Brand Blue" is `brandBlue`), read as `\${theme.colors.brandBlue}`. |\n| `textStyles` | Every named text style by key, read as `\${theme.text.title.fontSize}` and named by a text\'s style (`"style": "title"`, or `{"from": "title", ...}` to change some of its fields). A style may itself start `from` another and name `colors`; `textStyle` gives it resolved. |\n| `dark` | The colors for dark mode: the tokens and `colors` that differ from the light ones (its other fields are not used). |\n| `media` | The theme by screen size, as CSS media queries over custom properties: each rule\'s `patch` is a theme\'s JSON (`{"textStyles": {"display": {"fontSize": 40}}, "colors": {...}}`) merged over this one while the screen meets its conditions (`atScreen`). A type scale that changes at a breakpoint is written once here, not on every text. |\n| `primary` | Primary buttons and info toasts. |\n| `onPrimary` | Text on `primary`. |\n| `surface` | Dialog backgrounds. |\n| `onSurface` | Text on `surface`. |\n| `error` | Destructive buttons and error toasts. |\n| `success` | Success toasts. |\n| `warning` | Warning toasts. |\n| `fontFamily` | Font family of body text and buttons. |\n| `titleFontFamily` | Font family of titles. |\n| `radius` | Corner radius of dialogs. |\n| `buttonRadius` | Corner radius of buttons. |'),
      DocSection('theme-named-colours-and-styles', 'Named colours and styles', '- **Colours**: `colors` maps a name to `"#AARRGGBB"` (or to another colour\'s name: `"accent": "ember"`). Wherever a\n  colour is accepted, write its name. The roles `primary`, `onPrimary`, `surface`, `onSurface`, `error`, `success`,\n  `warning` (keys of the theme) are names too.\n- **Text styles**: `textStyles` maps a name to a TextStyle. A style may start `from` another and name colours. A\n  text names its style in one field, `"style": "title"`; to change some fields of it, `"style": {"from": "title",\n  "color": "ember"}` (`textTheme.titleLarge.merge(...)`: the fields written win). Runs, a button\'s `textStyle` and\n  an input\'s styles take the same two forms.\n- Changing a colour or style in the theme changes every node that names it, and only those.\n- In a binding a name is not read: bind the value, `"\${theme.colors.ember}"` or `"\${theme.text.title}"`; inside\n  a formula, `\${= done ? theme.colors.sage : theme.colors.mist}`.'),
      DocSection('theme-what-controls-take-from-the-theme', 'What controls take from the theme', 'A control\'s colours, fonts and shapes that its props leave unset come from the theme: `primary` fills filled buttons\n(labelled in `onPrimary`) and draws checks, thumbs, focus rings and text-button labels where it reads on `surface`\n(else `onSurface` does); `fontFamily` is every control label\'s font (`titleFontFamily` titles\'); `buttonRadius`\nshapes every kind of button and chip, `radius` dialogs, menus and pickers. Without a theme, controls are neutral:\nink on paper (near-black on white; near-white on near-black in dark mode) and the greys between, in no font of\ntheir own. Nothing comes from Material\'s defaults (no purple, ripples or elevation) or from the host app\'s theme.'),
      DocSection('theme-spacing-and-radius-scales', 'Spacing and radius scales', 'The theme has no spacing or radius tokens for nodes: its `radius` and `buttonRadius` shape controls only. Write\npadding, gaps and corner radii as numbers, or keep a scale as a project variable (`{"name": "space", "type": "map",\n"value": {"sm": 8, "md": 16, "lg": 32}}` in `site.json`) and bind it where it varies: `"bind": {"layout.padding":\n"\${space.md}", "props.spacing": "\${space.sm}"}`.'),
      DocSection('theme-a-type-scale-that-changes-with-the-screen-size', 'A type scale that changes with the screen size', 'The theme\'s `media` rules patch the theme as a node\'s rules patch a node: `{"minWidth": 1024, "patch":\n{"textStyles": {"title": {"fontSize": 56}}}}` makes every text using `title` grow at desktop width, written once. A\nnode\'s own media rule may switch its style (`"patch": {"props": {"style": "caption"}}`, which replaces the style)\nor change some fields (`{"style": {"fontSize": 20}}`, merged over the named style).'),
      DocSection('theme-dark-mode', 'Dark mode', '`"dark": {"colors": {"ink": "#FFEEEEEE"}}` gives the colours (and roles: `surface`, `primary`...) that differ in\ndark mode; everything naming `ink` follows the mode: fills, strokes, named text styles (a style whose `color` is\n`"ink"`), and the controls, which take the theme\'s roles. A style with a literal colour (`"#FF111111"`) does not\nchange: name the colour.\n\nWhich mode shows is the theme\'s `mode` (Flutter\'s `ThemeMode`, as `MaterialApp.themeMode`): `system` (the default:\nthe device\'s setting), `light` or `dark`. A site\'s own switch is one action:\n\n```json\n{"type": "setThemeMode", "mode": "\${= theme.isDark ? \'light\' : \'dark\'}"}\n```\n\n`mode` is an expression giving `system`, `light` or `dark`. Every screen of the site redraws at once, the next page\nopens in the same mode, and with `persist` (the default) the choice is kept in the site\'s local storage, so a\nreload starts in it; `"persist": false` keeps it for this visit only. `\${theme.mode}` reads the mode chosen and\n`\${theme.isDark}` (also `\${screen.isDark}`) whether the screen is dark; bind a switch\'s value to\n`\${theme.isDark}` to show it. A theme without `dark` stays as designed in dark mode (its colours and controls light),\nwhile `\${theme.isDark}` still says dark (`\${theme.hasDark}` is false), so a page may choose its own colours.\n\nThe render command captures either: `--theme light` or `--theme dark` (the PNG names end `-light`, `-dark`), and a\n`--tap` on the switch afterwards captures the other.'),
      DocSection('theme-text', 'Text', 'A `text` node has `props.text` and `props.style`. What a text looks like when the style leaves something out: no\n`color`, white; no `fontSize`, 12; no `fontWeight`, 400; no `fontFamily`, the platform\'s default (Roboto on Android\nand the web); no `height`, the nearest `defaultTextStyle`\'s (a node key, Flutter\'s `DefaultTextStyle`, for its\nwhole subtree), else the font\'s own line height. Sizing: one line `{"hug": n}` × `{"hug": n}`; a paragraph `{"fill": n}` wide × `{"hug": n}` high. A\nfixed height shorter than the lines clips them (`text_clipped`).\n\n`runs` style parts of the text: `[{"start": 0, "end": 5, "style": {"fontWeight": 700}}]` (character offsets, end\nexclusive, `\\n` counting as one), merged over `style`; a run may carry a `"link"` URL. A literal `\$` right before an\nexpression is text: `"\$\${price}"` shows `\$47`. There is no escape for a literal `\${`: compute it.'),
      DocSection('theme-superscripts-and-a-raised-currency-sign', 'Superscripts and a raised currency sign', 'A raised or lowered character (a price\'s "\$", a footnote mark): a run with `"fontFeatures": ["sups"]` (or `"subs"`)\nwhen the font has those OpenType features; otherwise a smaller `fontSize` in a row of texts aligned\n`crossAxisAlignment: start` (or `baseline`) for the exact shift.'),
      DocSection('theme-fonts', 'Fonts', '`style.fontFamily` names a family (`"Inter"`), with `fontWeight` and `fontStyle` choosing the file. A site declares\nthe families it ships in `site.json`, in the shape of a Flutter pubspec\'s `fonts:` section, the files beside it:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "pages": ["home.json"],\n  "fonts": [\n    {"family": "Fraunces", "fonts": [\n      {"asset": "fonts/fraunces-latin-400-normal.woff"},\n      {"asset": "fonts/fraunces-latin-700-normal.woff", "weight": 700},\n      {"asset": "fonts/fraunces-latin-400-italic.woff", "style": "italic"}\n    ]}\n  ],\n  "theme": {"fontFamily": "Fraunces", "textStyles": {"body": {"fontFamily": "Fraunces", "fontSize": 17}}}\n}\n```\n\n- `family` is the name text styles use, whatever the file calls itself; each file has a `weight` (100–900, default\n  400) and a `style` (`normal` or `italic`).\n- Files are `.ttf`, `.otf` or `.woff` (an npm `@fontsource/<family>` package\'s `files/` folder has a `.woff` beside\n  each `.woff2`). WOFF2 is not read (`font_format`); a declared file that is not there is `font_missing`.\n- The render command loads them with no flag, before the page shows; a published site loads them from its files.\n- A family a text style names that no file provides is `font_fallback`, naming the nodes that use it: declare it,\n  or pass `--fonts <dir>` (`--fonts system` for the system\'s fonts). A family nobody declared is fetched by name\n  from Google Fonts in an app.\n\nCharacters the font has no glyph for draw as empty boxes (`missing_glyph`): use an `icon`.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'decoration',
    title: 'Decoration, images, icons and drawing',
    summary: 'What a node\'s box paints beyond the base: gradients, pixel patterns and grain, borders on some sides, shadows and blurs, scrims over children, images, icons, SVG-like paths and custom drawing.',
    when: 'What a node\'s box paints beyond the base: gradients, pixel patterns and grain, borders on some sides, shadows and\nblurs, scrims over children, images, icons, SVG-like paths and custom drawing.',
    example: 'A card with a solid fill, a border, rounded corners and a shadow, and a gradient band:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["deco"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "deco": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "row"},\n      "layout": {"width": 520, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF9FAFB"}]}\n    },\n    "row": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["card", "gradient", "outlined"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 520}, "height": {"fill": 200}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 24, "mainAxisAlignment": "center"}\n    },\n    "card": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {\n        "fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}],\n        "radius": 12,\n        "effects": [{"type": "dropShadow", "color": "#33000000", "offset": [0, 4], "blurRadius": 16}]\n      }\n    },\n    "gradient": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {\n        "fills": [\n          {\n            "type": "radial",\n            "stops": [{"position": 0, "color": "#FFFDE68A"}, {"position": 1, "color": "#FFF97316"}]\n          }\n        ],\n        "radius": [24, 4, 24, 4]\n      }\n    },\n    "outlined": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 140, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {"strokes": [{"color": "#FF2563EB"}], "strokeWidth": 2, "dashPattern": [6, 4], "radius": 12}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- An effect needs its `type`; without it the effect is dropped.\n- Colours are `"#AARRGGBB"`, `"#RRGGBB"` or a theme name; `"#FFF"`, `rgb()` and CSS names are not read.\n- A `path` node without a `viewBox` is drawn in its box\'s own pixels from the top left and is not clipped to the\n  box (as Flutter\'s `CustomPaint`): give it a `viewBox` to scale it, or clip an ancestor (`path_overflow`).\n- Decoration on a type that draws no box (a `text`, a `listView`) is ignored (`decoration_ignored`): wrap it.\n- `clip` is needed for children to follow rounded corners.\n- A child\'s fill covers its parent\'s inside border: pad the parent, stroke outside, or move the border to the child.',
    words: 4097,
    items: ['icon', 'path', 'customPaint', 'imageLoading', 'imageLoaded', 'imageError'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('decoration-decoration-fields', 'Decoration fields', 'A node\'s `"decoration"`: what its box paints. Types without a box decoration keep only blur effects. Fills paint\nbottom to top under the node\'s content; `foregroundFills` paint over it, children included. Every colour may be a\ntheme colour\'s name.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `fills` | List<[Paint](decoration.md#type-Paint)> | `[]` |  | Paints for the box, bottom to top: a colour, a gradient, an image or noise. |\n| `strokes` | List<[Paint](decoration.md#type-Paint)> | `[]` |  | Paints for the border, drawn `strokeWidth` wide. |\n| `strokeWidth` | double | `1` | ≥ 0 | The border\'s width in pixels. Without `strokes` it draws nothing. |\n| `strokeAlign` | [StrokeAlign](values.md#enum-StrokeAlign) | `"inside"` | `inside`, `center`, `outside` |  |\n| `strokeSides` | [StrokeSides](values.md#enum-StrokeSides) | `"all"` |  | Which sides the border is drawn on: `all`, `top`, `bottom`, `left`, `right`, `topBottom`, `leftRight`... |\n| `strokeCap` | [StrokeCap](values.md#enum-StrokeCap) | `"butt"` | `butt`, `round`, `square` |  |\n| `dashPattern` | List<double> | `[]` |  | Dash and gap lengths, alternating; empty is a solid stroke. |\n| `radius` | [BorderRadius](values.md#type-BorderRadius) | `0` |  |  |\n| `effects` | List<[Effect](decoration.md#type-Effect)> | `[]` |  | Shadows and blurs: each `{"type": "dropShadow" \\| "innerShadow" \\| "layerBlur" \\| "backgroundBlur", ...}`. |\n| `clip` | [Clip](values.md#enum-Clip) | `"none"` | `none`, `hardEdge`, `antiAlias`, `antiAliasWithSaveLayer` | Clips the content to the box (rounded by `radius`). |\n| `blendMode` | [BlendMode](values.md#enum-BlendMode) | `"srcOver"` |  |  |\n| `foregroundFills` | List<[Paint](decoration.md#type-Paint)> | `[]` |  | Fills painted over the content. |\n| `shape` | [DecorationShape](values.md#enum-DecorationShape) | `"rectangle"` | `rectangle`, `circle` | A rectangle (rounded by `radius`) or a circle. |'),
      DocSection('decoration-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-imageLoading"></a>`imageLoading` | A node\'s image fill started loading, became ready, or failed. `\${result.url}` identifies the image and `\${result.status}` is `loading`, `loaded`, or `error`. Cached images can report loaded immediately without a loading event. |\n| <a id="trigger-imageLoaded"></a>`imageLoaded` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-imageError"></a>`imageError` |  |'),
      DocSection('decoration-gradients', 'Gradients', 'As Flutter\'s `LinearGradient`, a linear gradient runs from `"begin"` to `"end"` (alignments; default left to\nright; `[0, -1]` to `[0, 1]` is top to bottom). As `RadialGradient`, a radial one has a `"center"` and a `"radius"`\n(a share of the box\'s shortest side); past the last stop it keeps that stop\'s colour, so end a glow on a transparent\nstop. `transform` is the general form. A paint without `type` is an image if it has `image`, a linear gradient if it\nhas `stops`, else a solid colour.'),
      DocSection('decoration-a-pattern-in-pixels-a-background-grid-grain', 'A pattern in pixels, a background grid, grain', '**A pattern in pixels** (CSS `repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, #E5E7EB 0 1px, transparent 1px 80px)`): a\nlinear gradient with `"length": 80` (px from `begin` toward `end`) and `"tileMode": "repeated"`; a background grid is\ntwo of them, one `topCenter` → `bottomCenter`, one `centerLeft` → `centerRight`.\n\n```json\n"fills": [\n  {"type": "linear", "begin": "topCenter", "end": "bottomCenter", "length": 80, "tileMode": "repeated",\n   "stops": [{"position": 0, "color": "#14FFFFFF"}, {"position": 0.0125, "color": "#14FFFFFF"}, {"position": 0.0125, "color": "#00FFFFFF"}, {"position": 1, "color": "#00FFFFFF"}]},\n  {"type": "linear", "begin": "centerLeft", "end": "centerRight", "length": 80, "tileMode": "repeated",\n   "stops": [{"position": 0, "color": "#14FFFFFF"}, {"position": 0.0125, "color": "#14FFFFFF"}, {"position": 0.0125, "color": "#00FFFFFF"}, {"position": 1, "color": "#00FFFFFF"}]}\n]\n```\n\n**Grain**: `{"type": "noise", "noise": {"baseFrequency": 0.8, "numOctaves": 3, "seed": 1}, "color": "#FF000000",\n"opacity": 0.08}`, SVG\'s `feTurbulence` as a paint (a seamless tile repeated over the box; `blendMode` as CSS\n`mix-blend-mode`).'),
      DocSection('decoration-borders-rules-and-shadows', 'Borders, rules and shadows', 'A node\'s border is painted with its own box, **under its children**: a child with a fill covers an `inside` border\n(the default). Give the parent padding of the border\'s width, set `"strokeAlign": "outside"`, or put the border (or\nthe rule) on the filled child. `strokes` with `strokeWidth` (default 1), `strokeAlign` (`inside`, `center`, `outside`), `strokeSides` (`all`,\n`bottom`, `topBottom`...) and `dashPattern` (`[6, 4]`). A rule under a text: the text inside a `row` or `column`\nwith `"strokes": [{"color": ...}], "strokeSides": "bottom"`, or a `box` 1 high. `strokeWidth` without `strokes`\ndraws nothing. Effects: `dropShadow`, `innerShadow`, `layerBlur`, `backgroundBlur` (frosted glass), each with\n`color`, `offset`, `blurRadius`, `spreadRadius`.'),
      DocSection('decoration-a-scrim-over-a-photo', 'A scrim over a photo', '`foregroundFills` paint over the node **and its children**, as Flutter\'s `foregroundDecoration`: a scrim there\ndarkens a caption inside the node too. For a caption over a photo, paint the photo in `fills` and put the darkening\ngradient on a child `box` before the caption (a stack: photo box, gradient box, caption text), or on the photo\nbox\'s `foregroundFills` when the caption is a sibling painted after it.'),
      DocSection('decoration-images', 'Images', 'Images are image fills: `{"type": "image", "image": {"url": "...", "fit": "cover"}}` in `decoration.fills` of a box\n(give the box the image\'s size or an `aspectRatio`), placed as Flutter\'s `DecorationImage` places them: `fit` is a\n`BoxFit` (`cover`, `contain`, `fill`, `fitWidth`, `fitHeight`, `none`, `scaleDown`) and `alignment` an `Alignment`\n(`[0, -0.3]` keeps a face in a cropped photo). The `url` is one of:\n\n- **a file beside the site**, by its path relative to `site.json`\'s folder (`"images/hero.jpg"`, as a Flutter app\n  names an asset): PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, BMP or SVG. The render command reads it from the folder; a published site\n  from its files. A path that names no file is `image_failed`, naming it. Use this for photos and illustrations.\n- `https://...`: loaded by the app; the render command does not fetch it (`image_network`).\n- `data:image/...` (an SVG may be written inline as `data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg ...>`, URL-encoded).\n\nFills stack, first at the bottom: a photo with a gradient scrim over it, so text reads on it, is two fills:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["story"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "story": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 320},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["card"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 320}, "padding": 24}\n    },\n    "card": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["kicker", "headline"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 240, "padding": 20},\n      "props": {"mainAxisAlignment": "end", "crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 6},\n      "decoration": {\n        "radius": 16,\n        "clip": "antiAlias",\n        "fills": [\n          {"type": "image", "image": {"url": "assets/photo.png", "fit": "cover", "alignment": [0, -0.3]}},\n          {\n            "type": "linear",\n            "begin": [0, -1],\n            "end": [0, 1],\n            "stops": [{"color": "#00000000", "position": 0.35}, {"color": "#CC000000", "position": 1}]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    "kicker": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 302}, "height": {"hug": 16}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "TRAVEL",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 12, "fontWeight": 700, "letterSpacing": 2, "color": "#FFFDE68A"}\n      }\n    },\n    "headline": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 302}, "height": {"hug": 56}},\n      "props": {\n        "text": "A week on the salt marsh, by boat and on foot",\n        "style": {"fontSize": 20, "fontWeight": 700, "height": 1.3, "color": "#FFFFFFFF"}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```'),
      DocSection('decoration-illustration', 'Illustration', 'Three ways to draw art without a photo, each scaled to its box:\n\n- **An SVG file** (`images/hills.svg`) as an image fill: drawn as vectors at any size, `fit` and `alignment` as\n  for a photo. For a single shape or mark, a `path` node with SVG path data and a `viewBox`.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["hero"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "hero": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 340},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["art", "badge"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 340}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "art": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 214},\n      "decoration": {\n        "radius": 12,\n        "clip": "antiAlias",\n        "fills": [{"type": "image", "image": {"url": "assets/hills.svg", "fit": "cover"}}]\n      }\n    },\n    "badge": {\n      "type": "path",\n      "layout": {"width": 48, "height": 48},\n      "props": {\n        "data": "M12 2 L15 9 L22 9 L16.5 13.5 L18.5 21 L12 16.5 L5.5 21 L7.5 13.5 L2 9 L9 9 Z",\n        "viewBox": [24, 24]\n      },\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF4B740"}]}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- **`customPaint`**: draw lists in a view box, Flutter\'s `Canvas` calls as data (`rect`, `circle`, `path` with SVG\n  data, `line`, `repeat` over a count with `\${index}`), behind (`painter`) or over (`foregroundPainter`) the node\'s\n  content. Values may be expressions, so a drawing can follow data. It is not\n  clipped by the box\'s `radius`: round a parent with `clip` for that.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["hero"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "hero": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "page"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 260},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "page": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["scene"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 260}, "padding": 24}\n    },\n    "scene": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 212},\n      "customPaint": {\n        "viewBox": [320, 200],\n        "fit": "cover",\n        "painter": [\n          {"op": "rect", "rect": [0, 0, 320, 200], "paint": "#FFE8F1F8"},\n          {"op": "circle", "c": [236, 62], "radius": 28, "paint": "#FFF4B740"},\n          {\n            "op": "repeat",\n            "count": 3,\n            "ops": [\n              {\n                "op": "circle",\n                "c": ["\${= 60 + index * 34}", "\${= 48 + index * 6}"],\n                "radius": 3,\n                "paint": "#FF5D6D7E"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            "op": "path",\n            "d": "M0 150 C60 100 120 110 170 140 C220 170 270 120 320 130 L320 200 L0 200 Z",\n            "paint": "#FF7FB685"\n          },\n          {\n            "op": "path",\n            "d": "M0 170 C80 140 160 160 220 175 C260 185 290 170 320 165 L320 200 L0 200 Z",\n            "paint": "#FF3E7C59"\n          },\n          {\n            "op": "line",\n            "p1": [40, 196],\n            "p2": [280, 196],\n\n(Continues: decoration.md#decoration-illustration.)'),
      DocSection('decoration-icons', 'Icons', 'An `icon` node with `props.icon` set to a Material icon name (`"check_circle"`, `"menu"`, `"north_east"`; any name\nat fonts.google.com/icons; `_outlined`, `_rounded`, `_sharp` pick the style), `props.color` and `props.size` (the\nglyph\'s size, centered in the node\'s box; without it the glyph fills the box). A text field\'s\n`decoration.prefixIcon` is `{"icon": "search", "size": 18}`. A name the renderer does not know draws nothing\n(`icon_not_drawn`).'),
      DocSection('decoration-small-marks-and-shapes', 'Small marks and shapes', 'A mark the font lacks (✦, ✳): an `icon` (`"auto_awesome"`, `"star"`), or a `path` node with SVG path data and a\n`viewBox` so it scales to its box: the one decorated shape (fills, strokes and shadows from its `decoration`). Custom\ndrawing beyond one path (several shapes, a line through points, shapes in different colors, text on a canvas): the\n`customPaint` behavior\'s draw lists, behind or over the node\'s content. A line through points is a `path` op with\n`points` (a formula of `\${size.width}` for a share of the box), or with `commands` (Flutter\'s `Path` calls:\n`moveTo`, `lineTo`, `quadraticBezierTo`, `cubicTo`, `close`) for curves; shapes in different colors are one `path`\nop per color.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'forms',
    title: 'Buttons, forms and inputs',
    summary: 'Buttons, text fields, checkboxes, switches, radios, sliders, dropdowns, segmented buttons, date and time pickers, chips and signatures: every control\'s props, **how to style each one (in one place, below)**, two-way binding to a variable, validation and error states, focus and the keyboard.',
    when: 'Buttons, text fields, checkboxes, switches, radios, sliders, dropdowns, segmented buttons, date and time pickers,\nchips and signatures: every control\'s props, **how to style each one (in one place, below)**, two-way binding to a\nvariable, validation and error states, focus and the keyboard.',
    example: 'An email field stored in a variable on every change, an error shown after a failed send, and a thank-you after a\ngood one:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["contact"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "contact": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 500},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["email", "emailError", "send", "thanks"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 500}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 8, "crossAxisAlignment": "start"}\n    },\n    "email": {\n      "type": "textField",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 56},\n      "props": {"decoration": {"labelText": "Email", "hintText": "you@example.com"}, "keyboardType": "emailAddress"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "changed"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "email", "value": "\${result}"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "emailError": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 18}},\n      "props": {"text": "Enter a valid email address.", "style": {"fontSize": 13, "color": "#FFDC2626"}},\n      "bind": {"visible": "\${= tried && !contains(email, \'@\')}"}\n    },\n    "send": {\n      "type": "elevatedButton",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": 44},\n      "props": {"label": "Send"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [\n            {"type": "setVariable", "variable": "tried", "value": "true"},\n            {\n              "type": "if",\n              "condition": {"left": "\${= contains(email, \'@\')}", "op": "isTrue"},\n              "then": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "sent", "value": "true"}]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "thanks": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "Thanks! We\'ll reply within a day.", "style": {"fontSize": 15, "color": "#FF16A34A"}},\n      "bind": {"visible": "\${sent}"}\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "contact": [\n      {"name": "email", "type": "text", "value": ""},\n      {"name": "tried", "type": "boolean", "value": false},\n      {"name": "sent", "type": "boolean", "value": false}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- A button\'s text is `label`, not `text`; its colours are in `style`, not `decoration`.\n- A hugging button is only as wide as its label, without padding.\n- An input does nothing with its value until a `changed` reaction stores it, or its value prop is bound.\n- `\${result}` in a `changed` chain is the new value until an action that gives a value replaces it; `setVariable`\n  does not.\n- Every action key is written flat in the action; a misspelled one is dropped (`unknown_action_key`).\n- The `validator` prop is not applied: validate with variables.\n- An outlined border without `contentPadding` puts the text on the border.',
    words: 10159,
    items: ['filledButton', 'elevatedButton', 'outlinedButton', 'textButton', 'iconButton', 'floatingActionButton', 'textField', 'checkbox', 'switch', 'radio', 'slider', 'dropdown', 'segmentedButton', 'datePicker', 'timePicker', 'dateTimeInput', 'signature', 'chip', 'actionChip', 'choiceChip', 'filterChip', 'inputChip', 'changed', 'changeEnd', 'submitted', 'editingComplete', 'focusGained', 'focusLost', 'keyDown', 'keyUp', 'editText', 'focus'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('forms-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-changed"></a>`changed` | An input\'s value changed (typed text, a toggled checkbox, a slider step, a picked item). `\${result}` is the new value (a text field\'s: its text, word and selection). |\n| <a id="trigger-changeEnd"></a>`changeEnd` | A slider was let go, with its final value. |\n| <a id="trigger-submitted"></a>`submitted` | A text field was submitted from the keyboard. |\n| <a id="trigger-editingComplete"></a>`editingComplete` | A text field lost focus after editing. |\n| <a id="trigger-focusGained"></a>`focusGained` | A text field gained or lost focus. |\n| <a id="trigger-focusLost"></a>`focusLost` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-keyDown"></a>`keyDown` | A key went down (or up) while the screen shows; `Trigger.key` limits it to one key or combination, `Trigger.when` to while a formula holds. `\${result.key}`, `\${result.shift}`, `\${result.alt}`, `\${result.meta}`. |\n| <a id="trigger-keyUp"></a>`keyUp` |  |'),
      DocSection('forms-styling-the-controls-in-one-place', 'Styling the controls, in one place', '| Control | Its look | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| `textField` | label, hint, helper and error texts and their styles; border (`"border": {"type": "outline", "borderSide": {"color": ..., "width": 1}, "borderRadius": 8}`), `enabledBorder`, `focusedBorder`, `errorBorder`, `focusedErrorBorder`; `fillColor` + `filled`; `contentPadding`; `prefixIcon` / `suffixIcon`, `prefixText` / `suffixText` | `props.decoration` ([InputDecoration](#type-InputDecoration), [InputBorder](#type-InputBorder), [InputIcon](#type-InputIcon)) |\n| `textField` | the typed text\'s style (`style`), alignment, the caret (`cursorColor`, `showCursor`), the focus ring (`focusRingColor`, `focusRingWidth`) | `props` ([textField](#node-textField)) |\n| buttons | `backgroundColor`, `foregroundColor`, `textStyle` (the label\'s size and weight), `shape` (`{"type": "roundedRectangle", "borderRadius": 10}`), `side` (border), `padding`, `elevation` | `props.style` ([ButtonStyle](#type-ButtonStyle)) |\n| `checkbox` | `activeColor`, `checkColor`, `fillColor`, `side` / `activeSide` (the box\'s border), `borderRadius`, `compact` | `props` ([checkbox](#node-checkbox)) |\n| `switch` | `activeTrackColor`, `inactiveTrackColor`, `activeThumbColor`, `inactiveThumbColor`, `fillTrack`, `thumbInset`, `trackOutlineWidth`, `trackRadius` | `props` ([switch](#node-switch)) |\n| `radio`, `slider`, `dropdown`, `segmentedButton` | their colours, track and thumb shapes | `props` ([radio](#node-radio), [slider](#node-slider), [dropdown](#node-dropdown), [segmentedButton](#node-segmentedButton)) |\n| a labelled row | a `row` holding the control (with `"ignorePointer": true` and its value bound) and a text, with the row\'s `click` reaction | [a labelled checkbox](#forms-a-labelled-checkbox-or-switch) |\n\nEvery colour there may be a theme colour\'s name; every text style may name a theme style. An outlined field needs\n`"contentPadding": [14, 16, 14, 16]` in its decoration to keep its text off the border.'),
      DocSection('forms-a-text-field-bound-to-a-variable-two-way', 'A text field bound to a variable (two-way)', 'Bind its `props.initialValue` to the variable: `"bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${query}"}`. Typing sets the\nvariable (its `changed` reaction also runs), and setting the variable elsewhere (a clear button, a stepper,\n`--set`) changes the text, keeping the caret, as a `TextEditingController` held in state. The other inputs show\ntheir bound value prop (`"bind": {"props.value": "\${agree}"}` for a checkbox, switch, slider or dropdown,\n`props.selected` for a segmented button, `props.groupValue` for radios) and report a change through `changed`:\nstore `\${result}` in the same variable and the control follows it.'),
      DocSection('forms-validation-and-an-error-state', 'Validation and an error state', 'Keep the values in variables, set a `tried` flag on submit, and show errors from computed variables: bind\n`props.decoration.errorText` (the field turns to its `errorBorder` and shows the text) or a separate text\'s\n`visible`. An empty `errorText` shows no error. The `validator` prop is declared but not applied by the SDK; `inputFormatter` applies only\n`{"type": "regex", "pattern": ..., "allow": true}`.\n\n```json\n"variables": {"page_variables": [\n  {"name": "seats", "type": "text", "value": "10"},\n  {"name": "seatsError", "type": "text", "formula": "seats == \'\' || number(seats) < 1 ? \'Enter at least 1 seat.\' : \'\'"}\n]}\n```\n\n```json\n"seatsField": {"type": "textField", "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 72},\n  "bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${seats}", "props.decoration.errorText": "\${seatsError}"},\n  "props": {"keyboardType": "number", "decoration": {"labelText": "Seats",\n    "border": {"type": "outline", "borderRadius": 8}, "errorBorder": {"type": "outline", "borderRadius": 8, "borderSide": {"color": "#FFDC2626"}}}}}\n```\n\nGive a field that may show an error a hug height (`{"hug": 56}`): it grows by the error line, and the form with it;\na fixed height keeps the field that tall. A form submitted to a service: `submitForm` ([data](data.md#page-data)).'),
      DocSection('forms-a-stepper-around-a-field', 'A stepper around a field', 'Two icon buttons that `setVariable` with `"op": "add"` / `"subtract"` on a number, and a field bound two-way to the\nsame variable. Keep the last valid value in a second variable when the typed text may be invalid.'),
      DocSection('forms-a-clear-button-in-the-field', 'A clear button in the field', 'Its `decoration.suffixIcon` with a tap reaction (`actions` is a list of reactions, as a node\'s), shown only while\nthere is text by binding the icon:\n\n```json\n"search": {"type": "textField", "layout": {"width": {"fill": 280}, "height": 44},\n  "bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${query}", "props.decoration.suffixIcon.icon": "\${= query == \'\' ? \'\' : \'close\'}"},\n  "props": {"decoration": {"hintText": "Search dishes", "prefixIcon": {"icon": "search", "size": 18}, "suffixIcon": {"icon": "close", "size": 18,\n    "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "query", "value": ""}]}]}}}}\n```'),
      DocSection('forms-a-labelled-checkbox-or-switch', 'A labelled checkbox or switch', 'The whole row toggles: the control ignores the pointer and shows the variable; the row\'s reaction toggles it. A tap\non a control inside a tappable row otherwise runs the control\'s own reaction only (the innermost wins).\n\n```json\n"agreeRow": {"type": "row", "children": ["agreeBox", "agreeText"], "props": {"spacing": 8},\n  "layout": {"width": {"hug": 240}, "height": 40},\n  "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "agree", "op": "toggle"}]}]},\n"agreeBox": {"type": "checkbox", "ignorePointer": true, "layout": {"width": 24, "height": 24}, "bind": {"props.value": "\${agree}"}},\n"agreeText": {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "I agree", "style": {"fontSize": 15, "color": "#FF111827"}},\n  "layout": {"width": {"hug": 60}, "height": {"hug": 20}}}\n```'),
      DocSection('forms-buttons', 'Buttons', 'Buttons (`filledButton`, `elevatedButton`, `outlinedButton`, `textButton`, `iconButton`) take `label` and `style`.\nTheir label text is 12 px unless `style.textStyle.fontSize` says otherwise. Give buttons a fixed or fill width. For\nfull control of a button\'s look (two lines, an icon after the label), use a `row` with a decoration, padding, text\nchildren, a `click` reaction and [hover and pressed states](interaction.md#interaction-hover-press-and-other-states).'),
      DocSection('forms-add-and-remove-items-a-list-editor', 'Add and remove items (a list editor)', 'Add: `setVariable` on the list with `"op": "add"` (appends; a list value appends each item) and\n`"value": "\${= object(\'name\', draft, \'done\', false)}"`, then clear the draft; guard it with the action\'s `when` (or\nan `if`) on the draft not being empty. Remove: in the item template, `"op": "removeAt"` with `"index": "\${index}"`.\nChange one item: `"op": "update"` with `index`, or a formula (`\${= updateWhere(habits, \'id\', item.id, h => set(h,\n\'done\', !h.done))}`). Give items an id (`newId(\'habit\')`) when they can be reordered or removed.'),
      DocSection('forms-focus-and-the-keyboard', 'Focus and the keyboard', '`focus` moves the focus to a field (or away), `editText` changes its text or selection. `submitted` fires on the\nkeyboard\'s done key; `textInputAction` picks the key. A canvas\'s `keyDown` reaction (`{"trigger": {"type":\n"keyDown", "key": "ArrowRight"}, ...}`) runs while no text field has the focus: arrow keys between tabs, Escape to\nclose. The render command types with `--type <id>=<text>` (it replaces the text) and presses keys with `--key`\n(after `--unfocus`).'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'lists',
    title: 'Lists, grids, tables and repeated data',
    summary: 'Anything repeated from data: lists and grids from one item template, nested lists (`item`, `index`, `parent`), equal-height card grids, tables, carousels (`pageView`), list tiles, pagination, pull to refresh, swipe actions and reordering.',
    when: 'Anything repeated from data: lists and grids from one item template, nested lists (`item`, `index`, `parent`),\nequal-height card grids, tables, carousels (`pageView`), list tiles, pagination, pull to refresh, swipe actions and\nreordering.',
    example: 'A `listView` repeats its first child once per item of its `data` binding; inside, `\${item}` is the item and\n`\${index}` its position:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["faq"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "faq": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 600},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["heading", "items"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 600}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12, "crossAxisAlignment": "start", "scrollable": true}\n    },\n    "heading": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 30}},\n      "props": {"text": "Questions", "style": {"fontSize": 24, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "items": {\n      "type": "listView",\n      "children": ["item"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 300}},\n      "props": {"scrollable": false, "spacing": 8},\n      "bind": {"data": "\${questions}"}\n    },\n    "item": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["q", "a"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 60}, "padding": 12},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 4},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF3F4F6"}], "radius": 8},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "open", "value": "\${= open == index ? -1 : index}"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "q": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 318}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "\${item.q}", "style": {"fontSize": 16, "fontWeight": 600, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "a": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 318}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "\${item.a}", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "height": 1.4, "color": "#FF4B5563"}},\n      "bind": {"visible": "\${= open == index}"}\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "faq": [\n      {"name": "open", "type": "integer", "value": -1},\n      {\n        "name": "questions",\n        "type": "list",\n        "value": [\n          {"q": "Can I cancel any time?", "a": "Yes. Your plan stays active until the end of the period."},\n          {"q": "Do you offer refunds?", "a": "Within 14 days of purchase, no questions asked."},\n          {"q": "Is there a free trial?", "a": "Every plan starts with 30 days free."}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Only the first child is the template; other children are ignored.\n- `item` and `index` are the innermost list\'s; the outer one is `parent`.\n- A list inside a scrolling page needs `"scrollable": false` (or `"physics": "never"`, which a `gridView` needs:\n  it has no `scrollable`), or it takes its design height and scrolls inside itself.\n- A wrapping `listView` runs along its `scrollDirection`: with the default `vertical` it flows top to bottom into\n  columns (`vertical_wrap`).\n- Decoration on a `listView` or `gridView` is ignored (`decoration_ignored`): put the list inside a column that has\n  it.\n- A `fill` height inside a hugging grid item is its design number (`fill_fallback`).\n- A slot inside a list of a component shows what the call passes in every item, built in the caller\'s scope: it\n  reads the caller\'s variables, not the item.',
    words: 6101,
    items: ['listView', 'gridView', 'pageView', 'tableView', 'listTile', 'pagination', 'reorderHandle', 'reorder', 'refresh', 'swipeAction', 'rowTap', 'paginate'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('lists-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-reorder"></a>`reorder` | A data list row was dragged to a new place by this node, its reorder handle (`\${result.from}`, `\${result.to}`). A list with a `reorder` fires it too, with `\${result.item}`, `\${result.fromList}`, `\${result.toList}`. |\n| <a id="trigger-refresh"></a>`refresh` | A list or grid was pulled past its start to refresh (its `pullToRefresh`, or its pagination\'s); its pagination reloads its first page too. A list with this reaction can always be pulled. |\n| <a id="trigger-swipeAction"></a>`swipeAction` | A swipe action of a list item ran (the list\'s `swipeActions`): `\${result.action}`, `\${result.label}`, `\${result.item}`, `\${result.index}`. |\n| <a id="trigger-rowTap"></a>`rowTap` | A table view\'s body row was tapped: `\${result.row}` (the row\'s data), `\${result.rowIndex}`, `\${result.column}` (the tapped column\'s key), `\${result.columnIndex}`. |'),
      DocSection('lists-one-template-from-data', 'One template from data', 'A `listView` (or `gridView`, `pageView`) repeats its **first child** once per item of its `data` binding:\n`"bind": {"data": "\${questions}"}`. Inside the repeated child, `\${item}` is the item (`\${item.title}`) and\n`\${index}` its position from 0. A list in a scrolling page sets `"scrollable": false` so it lays out every item at\nits full height; `spacing` separates items. Items fill the list\'s width. The item template can carry reactions: a\nclick on an item runs with that item\'s `item` and `index`. When the item is more than about five nodes, or appears\nelsewhere too, make it one call of a [component](components.md#page-components) (`"bind": {"props.plan": "\${item}"}`).'),
      DocSection('lists-a-grid-of-cards', 'A grid of cards', 'For cards in columns from one list inside a scrolling page, use a `gridView` with `minCrossAxisExtent` (CSS\n`repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))`: as many equal columns as fit), `"shrinkWrapRows": true` and\n`"physics": "never"` (it lays out every item and the page scrolls). A fixed number of columns: `crossAxisCount`. A\n`listView` with `"wrap": true` lays its items out at their own sizes in runs along its `scrollDirection`: set\n`"scrollDirection": "horizontal"` for chips or nav links side by side. In wrap mode the gap between items is\n`wrapSpacing` and between runs `runSpacing`; `spacing` does not apply.'),
      DocSection('lists-equal-height-cards', 'Equal-height cards', 'In a `gridView` with `"shrinkWrapRows": true` (CSS grid\'s auto rows) each row is as tall as its tallest item, and\nevery item is stretched to it, whether it hugs or fills its height. Make the item the card (the box with the\ndecoration): a card *inside* a hugging item column keeps its own height, and a card that fills the item\'s height\nthere takes its design number (`fill_fallback`). A banner above one card goes inside the card, with a top margin on\nthe others to line them up. A card\'s button pinned to its bottom: a `spacer` (or a `fill` height child) between the\ncontent and the button inside the stretched card. `shrinkWrapRows` wins over `mainAxisExtent` (`prop_ignored`); for\nrows at least n tall, give the item `"constraints": {"minHeight": n}`.'),
      DocSection('lists-nested-lists', 'Nested lists', 'A list inside a list\'s item repeats per item of its own `data`, usually a field of the outer item. Inside the inner\ntemplate `item` and `index` are the innermost list\'s; `parent` is the item around it (`\${parent.item}`,\n`\${parent.index}`, and its fields directly: `\${parent.name}`). Two levels:\n\n```json\n"sections": {"type": "listView", "children": ["section"], "bind": {"data": "\${= groupBy(dishes, \'section\')}"},\n             "props": {"scrollable": false, "spacing": 24}, "layout": {"width": {"fill": 600}, "height": {"hug": 400}}},\n"section":  {"type": "column", "children": ["sectionTitle", "dishList"], "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start"},\n             "layout": {"width": {"fill": 600}, "height": {"hug": 200}}},\n"sectionTitle": {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "\${item.key} (\${item.count})", "style": {"fontSize": 20, "color": "#FF111827"}},\n             "layout": {"width": {"hug": 200}, "height": {"hug": 24}}},\n"dishList": {"type": "listView", "children": ["dish"], "bind": {"data": "\${item.items}"}, "props": {"scrollable": false},\n             "layout": {"width": {"fill": 600}, "height": {"hug": 120}}},\n"dish":     {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "\${parent.key} \${parent.index}: \${item.name} (#\${index})", "style": {"color": "#FF374151"}},\n             "layout": {"width": {"fill": 600}, "height": {"hug": 20}}}\n```\n\nA third level reads the second\'s item as `parent`; to reach further out, carry the value down in the data.'),
      DocSection('lists-a-table-from-one-template', 'A table from one template', 'A `listView` of rows bound to the records, each row a label and a `gridView` of cells bound to `\${item.values}` with\n`crossAxisCount` the number of columns: one cell node for every column (the example in\n[a capped band](layout.md#layout-a-capped-band)). Four columns written by hand, or four lists side by side, are the same\ntable written four times. For a column that stays while the others scroll sideways, keep the label column a\n`listView` of its own beside one horizontally scrolling block of the cell grids, rows the same height in both. A\n`tableView` is a data table with columns declared once (sorting, row taps).'),
      DocSection('lists-a-weekly-grid', 'A weekly grid', 'Seven columns of days from data: a `gridView` with `"crossAxisCount": 7` bound to the days (`\${= range(7)}`, or a\ncomputed list of `{day, done}` records), each cell a box whose fill is bound to the item. Rows of habits × days: a\n`listView` of habits whose item holds a label and that 7-column grid bound to `\${item.days}`; in a cell, `\${parent}`\nis the habit and `\${index}` the day. A grid sizes its cells: set the cell height with `mainAxisExtent` and give\nthe cell `fill` on both axes (a fixed size is `fit_not_allowed`).\n\nA tap on a day flips it in the habit\'s record (`setAt` and `set` build the new list); the label counts the checks:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 400},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["habitList"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 400}, "padding": 24}\n    },\n    "habitList": {\n      "type": "listView",\n      "children": ["habit"],\n      "bind": {"data": "\${habits}"},\n      "props": {"scrollable": false, "spacing": 12},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 200}}\n    },\n    "habit": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["name", "week"],\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 6},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 70}}\n    },\n    "name": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "props": {"text": "\${item.name}: \${= count(item.days, d => d)}", "style": {"fontSize": 15, "color": "#FF111827"}},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}}\n    },\n    "week": {\n      "type": "gridView",\n      "children": ["day"],\n      "bind": {"data": "\${item.days}"},\n      "props": {"crossAxisCount": 7, "mainAxisExtent": 40, "crossAxisSpacing": 6, "physics": "never"},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 40}}\n    },\n    "day": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 40}, "height": {"fill": 40}},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFE5E7EB"}], "radius": 20},\n      "bind": {"decoration.fills[0].color": "\${= item ? \'#FF16A34A\' : \'#FFE5E7EB\'}"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [\n            {\n              "type": "setVariable",\n              "variable": "habits",\n              "value": "\${= setAt(habits, parent.index, set(parent.item, \'days\', setAt(parent.item.days, index, !item)))}"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "home": [\n      {\n        "name": "habits",\n        "type": "list",\n        "value": [\n          {"name": "Water", "days": [true, true, false, false, false, false, false]},\n          {"name": "Read", "days": [false, true, false, false, false, false, false]}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```'),
      DocSection('lists-a-carousel-pages-and-pagination', 'A carousel, pages and pagination', 'A `pageView` shows one item (or child) per page and swipes between them (`viewportFraction` below 1 shows the\nneighbours\' edges; `initialPage`). Long lists that load in pages: the list\'s `pagination` settings, with a\n`pagination` control or the `paginate` action to move between pages.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'navigation',
    title: 'Screens, navigation, modals and toasts',
    summary: 'Several screens and moving between them, a page\'s URL path, passing values to a screen, dialogs, bottom sheets and popovers, confirmations and toasts, app bars, navigation bars, tabs and disclosure (accordions).',
    when: 'Several screens and moving between them, a page\'s URL path, passing values to a screen, dialogs, bottom sheets\nand popovers, confirmations and toasts, app bars, navigation bars, tabs and disclosure (accordions).',
    example: 'Two screens: a list that opens a detail screen with a parameter, a modal, and a toast:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["home", "about", "signup"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "home": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "Home",\n      "slots": {"body": "homeCol"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "homeCol": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["toAbout", "openSignup", "toast"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12, "crossAxisAlignment": "start"}\n    },\n    "toAbout": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "About us"},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "navigate", "to": "about"}]}]\n    },\n    "openSignup": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Sign up"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "openModal", "to": "signup", "presentation": "dialog"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "toast": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Show a toast"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "showToast", "message": "Saved", "style": "success"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "about": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "About",\n      "path": "about",\n      "slots": {"body": "aboutCol"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 844},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFF9FAFB"}]}\n    },\n    "aboutCol": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["aboutTitle", "back"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 844}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12, "crossAxisAlignment": "start"}\n    },\n    "aboutTitle": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 30}},\n      "props": {"text": "About", "style": {"fontSize": 24, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "back": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 120, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Back"},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "navigate", "mode": "pop"}]}]\n    },\n    "signup": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "name": "Sign up",\n      "slots": {"body": "signupCol"},\n      "layout": {"width": 320, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}], "radius": 16}\n    },\n    "signupCol": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["signupTitle", "close"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 320}, "height": {"fill": 200}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 16}\n    },\n    "signupTitle": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 200}, "height": {"hug": 26}},\n      "props": {"text": "Join the waitlist", "style": {"fontSize": 20, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "close": {\n      "type": "filledButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 120, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Close"},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "closeModal"}]}]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- `to` names a canvas id; a screen that is not a root cannot be shown.\n- A modal shows its canvas at its design size: give the modal canvas the dialog\'s size, not the screen\'s.\n- `\${route.<param>}` exists only on the screen navigated to with `params`.\n- A canvas\'s `path` is a top-level key of the canvas node, not a prop.\n- Menus hidden behind `hovered` never open on touch screens.',
    words: 4166,
    items: ['appBar', 'navigationBar', 'bottomNavigationBar', 'tabs', 'tabBar', 'accordion', 'expansionTile', 'modal', 'load', 'backPressed', 'navigate', 'openModal', 'closeModal', 'showToast', 'confirm', 'openLink'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('navigation-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-load"></a>`load` | A screen appeared (set on its canvas). |\n| <a id="trigger-backPressed"></a>`backPressed` | On a screen (its canvas): the user tried to leave it (the system or browser back button, a back gesture, Escape on a dialog) while the canvas\'s `blockBack` holds (`props.blockBack`, usually bound: `\${= dirty}`). The screen stays and these actions run instead, e.g. a "Discard changes?" confirm that leaves with a navigate pop, which the block doesn\'t stop. While `blockBack` is false, back leaves as usual and this doesn\'t fire. |'),
      DocSection('navigation-screens', 'Screens', 'Each canvas in `roots` is a screen, unless canvases are grouped: canvases with the same `props.screen` are one\nscreen, one canvas per breakpoint ([a canvas per breakpoint](layout.md#layout-a-canvas-per-breakpoint)). A canvas is the\n`Scaffold` of its screen: put the page content in its `body` slot, usually a column filling it. Its\n`decoration.fills` is the page background; its `layout` is its design size (on a device the canvas takes the\nscreen\'s size).\n\nA site\'s pages may be separate documents (one file per page, checked and rendered together); `navigate` then names a\ncanvas id of another document. Give a canvas a `"path"` (`"pricing"`, a top-level key of the canvas node, not a\nprop) for its URL; without one it gets a path from its name. The first screen of the first document is the entry\nscreen.'),
      DocSection('navigation-going-to-a-screen-and-back', 'Going to a screen and back', '`{"type": "navigate", "to": "<canvas id>"}` pushes the screen; `"mode": "pop"` goes back; `"replace"` and `"reset"`\nreplace the history. For a screen with a canvas per breakpoint, name any of them. `"params": {"id": "\${item.id}"}`\npasses values the destination reads as `\${route.id}`. A link to the screen\'s path with a query string passes the same\n(`trip?id=coast`), and so does the render command\'s `--navigate trip?id=coast`. A screen opened without the param\nreads it as empty: give the page a default (`coalesce(find(trips, \'id\', route.id), first(trips))`).\n`transition` picks the animation (`fade`, `slideUp`...).'),
      DocSection('navigation-modals-and-toasts', 'Modals and toasts', '`{"type": "openModal", "to": "<canvas id>"}` shows another canvas over the screen, at its design size\n(`presentation`: `dialog`, `bottomSheet`, `fullScreen`, a popover anchored to a node...). Inside it,\n`{"type": "closeModal"}` closes it, and its value becomes the opener\'s `\${result}`. The modal canvas is a root like\nany screen; give it the size of the dialog. `{"type": "showToast", "message": "Saved", "style": "success"}` shows a\nshort message; `confirm` asks yes or no and runs `actions` or `cancelActions`.'),
      DocSection('navigation-a-mobile-menu-drawer', 'A mobile menu (drawer)', 'A menu button that toggles a `menuOpen` variable, and the menu a node bound `"visible": "\${menuOpen}"`. As an\noverlay over the page: the canvas body is a `stack` filling it, the page\'s scrolling column first and the menu\npanel last (fill width, placed at `"y": 64`), hidden unless open; or open it as a modal (`"presentation":\n"fullScreen"` or a sheet). A link in the menu closes it (`setVariable menuOpen false`) and navigates. The render\ncommand captures the open state with `--tap menuButton`; an overlay sized to the window is drawn in the first\nwindow of a `--full-page` capture.'),
      DocSection('navigation-tabs-and-an-accordion-faq', 'Tabs and an accordion (FAQ)', 'Tabs from a variable: a row of tab labels whose `selected` binds to `\${= tab == \'lunch\'}` with a click that sets\n`tab`, and the panels bound `visible` on `tab` (the `tabs` and `tabBar` node types do the same with Material\'s\nlook). An FAQ where several items may be open: a list variable of open indices; an item\'s click sets\n`\${= contains(open, index) ? without(open, index) : append(open, index)}`, its answer is visible while\n`\${= contains(open, index)}`, and its icon turns (`motion.rotate`) with a transition.'),
      DocSection('navigation-app-bars-and-navigation-bars', 'App bars and navigation bars', 'A canvas\'s `appBar` slot spans the top at its own height and `bottomNavigationBar` the bottom; the body sits\nbetween, and `floatingActionButton` sits 16 px from the right above the bottom bar. `navigationBar` and\n`bottomNavigationBar` take destinations (icon, label) and report the chosen index through `changed`.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'state',
    title: 'State and logic',
    summary: 'Variables and where they live, computed and function variables, expressions and every binding path with the value it expects, conditions, the formula functions (grouped: text, numbers, money, lists, objects, dates, colours), the actions that change state, and sandboxed scripts.',
    when: 'Variables and where they live, computed and function variables, expressions and every binding path with the value\nit expects, conditions, the formula functions (grouped: text, numbers, money, lists, objects, dates, colours), the\nactions that change state, and sandboxed scripts.',
    example: 'A counter: a variable, two buttons that change it, and a text and a colour bound to it.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["counter"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "counter": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 400},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["label", "total", "add"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 400}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12, "mainAxisAlignment": "center"}\n    },\n    "label": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"hug": 24}},\n      "props": {"text": "Clicked \${count} times", "style": {"fontSize": 18, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "total": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF6B7280"}},\n      "bind": {"props.text": "\${= \'Total: \' + money(count * price, \'\$\')}"}\n    },\n    "add": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 44},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF2563EB"}], "radius": 8},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "count", "op": "add", "value": "1"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "counter": [{"name": "count", "type": "integer", "value": 0}, {"name": "price", "type": "decimal", "value": 2.5}]\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- `\${false}` reads a variable called `false`: a literal is `\${= false}`.\n- Values in `props`, `layout` and `decoration` are literal: `"opacity": "\${x}"` is an error; bind it.\n- A backslash in a formula is written twice in JSON: `"\${= matches(code, \'^\\\\d{4}\$\')}"`.\n- A component never reads its caller\'s variables: pass them as parameters.\n- Per-breakpoint canvases have separate variables: shared state lives in `page_variables`.\n- A function variable named like a formula function is never called (the built-in wins).\n- Formula syntax errors and unknown names in formulas are reported by the render command (the SDK parses them).\n- A misspelled binding path is `unknown_bind_path`; a name nothing declares is `unknown_name`.',
    words: 6398,
    items: ['valueChanged', 'actionError', 'setVariable', 'setValue', 'setVariant', 'callFunction', 'if', 'forEach', 'delay', 'runScript', 'retryFailed'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('state-variables', 'Variables', 'Declare them in the document\'s `variables`, under a canvas id (that canvas only) or under `"page_variables"` (every\ncanvas of the document, kept while the user moves between them). A site\'s `site.json` adds project variables, read\nby bare name in every page and component. A variable\'s keys:\n\n| Key | Example | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `"v1"` |  |\n| `name` | `"count"` | Unique in its scope; what expressions read (`\${name}`). |\n| `type` | `"integer"` |  |\n| `value` | `3` | The default value, as `type` holds it (see `VariableType.coerce`); null when unset. |\n| `formula` | `"a + 1"` | The expression (what goes in `\${= ...}`) that computes the value of a computed variable; empty for a plain one. A computed variable is read-only: it changes when what its formula reads changes. |\n| `parameters` | `["a"]` | A computed variable with parameters is a function: formulas call it by name (`clamp01(x)`), and its `formula` reads the arguments by these names. |\n| `options` | `["a"]` | The options of a `VariableType.choice` variable. |\n| `persist` | `true` | Whether the app keeps the value on the device: it starts from the value it had last time (not `value`) and every change is saved. A draft, a list the user builds up. A computed variable can\'t persist (`persists`). |\n\nTypes:\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `integer` | A whole number (`int`). |\n| `text` | Text (`String`). |\n| `decimal` | A number with decimals (`double`). |\n| `boolean` | `true` or `false`. |\n| `color` | A color, `#AARRGGBB`. |\n| `list` | A JSON list. |\n| `map` | A JSON object. |\n| `image` | An image URL. |\n| `choice` | One of `Variable.options`, stored as the option\'s value. |'),
      DocSection('state-expressions', 'Expressions', '`\${name}` or `\${path}` reads a value: `\${count}`, `\${user.name}`, `\${items[0].price}`, `\${pal[item.kind]}`.\n`\${= formula}` computes one: arithmetic (`+ - * / %`), comparisons (`== != < <= > >=`), `&&`, `||`, `!`,\n`cond ? a : b`, literals (`\'text\'`, `3.5`, `true`, `null`, lists `[1, 2]`), and lambdas for list functions\n(`x => x.price`). A text that is exactly one expression gives its value with its type; inside other text a number is\nprinted without trailing zeros. Names an expression may start with, besides the variables: `data`, `route`, `storage`, `screen`, `theme`, `item`, `index`, `parent`, `result`, `loop`, `auth`, `drag`, `perf`, `track`, `dismiss`, `pan`, `transform`, `flip`, `tilt`, `view`, `sticky`, `script`, `speech`, `pageOffset`.'),
      DocSection('state-binding-paths', 'Binding paths', 'What each path of `bind` expects. A formula gives the value as the field is written in JSON: a number, `true` /\n`false`, a name for an enum, a list or an object for the fields written that way. A value of another shape is not\nread and the field keeps its value. Values are read loosely: `"12"` is a number, `1` and `"true"` are true.\n\n| Path | Type | A formula gives |\n|---|---|---|\n| `visible` | `bool` | `true` or `false` |\n| `opacity` | `double` | a number |\n| `selected` | `bool` | `true` or `false` |\n| `disabled` | `bool` | `true` or `false` |\n| `data` | `List` | a list |\n| `layout.width` | `AxisSize` | a number (fixed) or {"fill"\\|"flexible"\\|"hug"\\|"fixed": number} |\n| `layout.height` | `AxisSize` | a number (fixed) or {"fill"\\|"flexible"\\|"hug"\\|"fixed": number} |\n| `layout.constraints` | `BoxConstraints` | {"minWidth", "maxWidth", "minHeight", "maxHeight"} (each optional, numbers >= 0) |\n| `layout.margin` | `EdgeInsets` | a number (all sides) or [left, top, right, bottom] |\n| `layout.padding` | `EdgeInsets` | a number (all sides) or [left, top, right, bottom] |\n| `layout.aspectRatio` | `double` | a number |\n| `layout.flex` | `int` | a whole number |\n| `layout.squeezable` | `bool` | `true` or `false` |\n| `layout.x` | `AxisPosition` | a number (distance from the start) or {"start": d}, {"end": d}, {"start": a, "end": b}, {"align": -1..1}, {"relative": d} |\n| `layout.y` | `AxisPosition` | a number (distance from the start) or {"start": d}, {"end": d}, {"start": a, "end": b}, {"align": -1..1}, {"relative": d} |\n| `layout.align` | `Alignment` | [x, y] from -1 to 1, or a name: topLeft, topCenter, topRight, centerLeft, center, centerRight, bottomLeft, bottomCenter, bottomRight |\n| `layout.order` | `int` | a whole number |\n| `layout.basis` | `double` | a number |\n| `decoration.fills` | `List<Paint>` | a list of Paint objects |\n| `decoration.strokes` | `List<Paint>` | a list of Paint objects |\n| `decoration.strokeWidth` | `double` | a number |\n| `decoration.strokeAlign` | `StrokeAlign` | one of its names ([StrokeAlign](values.md#enum-StrokeAlign)) |\n| `decoration.strokeSides` | `StrokeSides` | one of its names ([StrokeSides](values.md#enum-StrokeSides)) |\n| `decoration.strokeCap` | `StrokeCap` | one of its names ([StrokeCap](values.md#enum-StrokeCap)) |\n| `decoration.dashPattern` | `List<double>` | a list of double objects |\n| `decoration.radius` | `BorderRadius` | a number (every corner), [x, y] (every corner elliptical) or [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] (each a number or [x, y]) |\n| `decoration.effects` | `List<Effect>` | a list of Effect objects |\n| `decoration.clip` | `Clip` | one of its names ([Clip](values.md#enum-Clip)) |\n| `decoration.blendMode` | `BlendMode` | one of its names ([BlendMode](values.md#enum-BlendMode)) |\n| `decoration.foregroundFills` | `List<Paint>` | a list of Paint objects |\n| `decoration.shape` | `DecorationShape` | one of its names ([DecorationShape](values.md#enum-DecorationShape)) |\n\n`props.<prop>` takes what the prop\'s type is written as: `"\${= open ? \'vertical\' : \'horizontal\'}"` for\n`props.direction`, a TextStyle object or a theme style\'s name for `props.style`. Every bindable field:\n\n\n(Continues: state.md#state-binding-paths.)'),
      DocSection('state-conditions', 'Conditions', 'An if / else-if / else rule. Its first branch whose test holds and that sets a property gives the property its value; when none does, the property keeps its binding\'s or its own value. JSON:\n\n```json\n{"id": "c1", "name": "Low stock", "branches": [\n  {"when": {"left": "\${stock}", "op": "lessThan", "right": "5"},\n   "set": [{"node": "badge", "path": "visible", "value": true}]},\n  {"set": [{"node": "badge", "path": "visible", "value": false}]}]}\n\n```\n\n- Branch: One branch: when `when` holds (always, for an `else`: null), the properties in `sets` take their values.\n- Set entry: Sets property `path` (a binding path, DESIGN.md §5.1) of node `node` to `value`: a JSON value, where a string is an expression read like a binding\'s (`\${= qty * 2}`, `#FF0000`, `Hello \${name}`).\n- Comparison: `left op right` (the right side only for ops that `ConditionOp.takesRight`).\n- Junction: All of `parts` (`and`) or any of them (`or`). Every part is evaluated. JSON: `{"and": [...]}` / `{"or": [...]}`.\n- Operand: One side of a `Comparison`: an expression text whose `\${...}` are read (`\${count}`, `\${= a + b}`, `3`, `done`), or, when `raw`, a literal taken as written. Both are then parsed loosely (`3` is a number, `true` a bool, `[1, 2]` a list). JSON: the text, or `{"raw": text}`.\n\n| op | Reads right | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `equalsTo` | yes |  |\n| `notEqualsTo` | yes |  |\n| `greaterThan` | yes |  |\n| `lessThan` | yes |  |\n| `greaterThanOrEqualTo` | yes |  |\n| `lessThanOrEqualTo` | yes |  |\n| `isEmpty` | no | Null, or an empty text, list or map. |\n| `isNotEmpty` | no |  |\n| `contains` | yes | A list holds the right operand, a text contains it, a map has it as a key. |\n| `isOdd` | no |  |\n| `isEven` | no |  |\n| `isNull` | no | Null, or the text `null`. |\n| `isTrue` | no |  |\n| `isFalse` | no |  |'),
      DocSection('state-scripts', 'Scripts', 'A document\'s sandboxed JavaScript (`scripts`), run by `runScript` or called from a formula (`script.name(...)`).\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `id` | String | `""` |  |  |\n| `name` | String | `""` |  | A JavaScript identifier: script.<name>(...). |\n| `description` | String | `""` |  |  |\n| `params` | Object | unset |  | [{"name", "description", "defaultValue"}]. |\n| `source` | String | `""` |  | JavaScript. |\n| `version` | int | `1` |  | Goes up each time the script is saved. |\n| `capabilities` | List<String> | `[]` |  | What it may do: variables.read, variables.write, nodes.read, navigation, api, cloud, actions, clock. |\n| `timeoutMs` | int | `1000` | ≥ 1 |  |\n| `memoryLimitMb` | int | `32` | ≥ 1 | Enforced on devices; on the web only `timeoutMs` applies. |\n| `pageId` | String | unset |  | Null: a project script. |\n| `tests` | Object | unset |  | Sample runs: [{"name", "args", "vars", "nodes", "expect", "expectError"}]. |'),
      DocSection('state-formula-functions', 'Formula functions', 'The functions a formula (`\${= ...}`) can call, from the SDK\'s formula engine, grouped.\n\n#### Text\n\n| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-left"></a>`left` | `left(text, count)` | `left("MX4821", 2) → MX` |\n| <a id="fn-right"></a>`right` | `right(text, count)` | `right("1FUJGLDR5MX4821", 6) → MX4821` |\n| <a id="fn-upper"></a>`upper` | `upper(text)` | `upper("hi") → HI` |\n| <a id="fn-lower"></a>`lower` | `lower(text)` | `lower("Hi") → hi` |\n| <a id="fn-trim"></a>`trim` | `trim(text)` | `trim("  hi ") → hi` |\n| <a id="fn-contains"></a>`contains` | `contains(text or list, value)` | `contains(lower(title), lower(search)) → true` |\n| <a id="fn-startsWith"></a>`startsWith` | `startsWith(text, prefix)` | `startsWith("Buy milk", "Buy") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-endsWith"></a>`endsWith` | `endsWith(text, suffix)` | `endsWith("photo.png", ".png") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-padLeft"></a>`padLeft` | `padLeft(value, width, char)` | `padLeft(4, 2) → 04 (numbers pad with 0, text with spaces)` |\n| `padLeft` | `padLeft(text, width, char?)` | `padLeft(42, 5, "0") → 00042` |\n| <a id="fn-padRight"></a>`padRight` | `padRight(value, width, char)` | `padRight("A", 3, ".") → A..` |\n| `padRight` | `padRight(text, width, char?)` | `padRight("ab", 4, ".") → ab..` |\n| <a id="fn-substring"></a>`substring` | `substring(text, start, end)` | `substring("Vinyl", 0, 3) → Vin` |\n| `substring` | `substring(text, start, end?)` | `substring("EX-102", 3) → 102` |\n| <a id="fn-replace"></a>`replace` | `replace(text, from, to)` | `replace("a-b-c", "-", " ") → a b c` |\n| `replace` | `replace(text, from, to)` | `replace("1,402", ",", "") → 1402` |\n| <a id="fn-regexReplace"></a>`regexReplace` | `regexReplace(text, pattern, to)` | `regexReplace("WILLOW PHARMACY 044", " [0-9]+\$", "") → WILLOW PHARMACY; \\\$1 in to inserts a group` |\n| <a id="fn-titleCase"></a>`titleCase` | `titleCase(text)` | `titleCase("SQ *KESTREL FLOWERS") → Sq *Kestrel Flowers` |\n| <a id="fn-split"></a>`split` | `split(text, separator)` | `split("rock, jazz", ", ") → [rock, jazz]` |\n| `split` | `split(text, separator?)` | `split("2481") → [2, 4, 8, 1]` |\n| <a id="fn-matches"></a>`matches` | `matches(text, pattern)` | `matches(code, "^\\d{4}\$") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-slug"></a>`slug` | `slug(text)` | `slug("Kind of Blue!") → kind-of-blue` |\n| <a id="fn-charCode"></a>`charCode` | `charCode(text, index)` | `charCode("MX", 1) → 88` |\n| <a id="fn-fromCharCode"></a>`fromCharCode` | `fromCharCode(code, …) or fromCharCode(list)` | `fromCharCode(65 + seat) → B` |\n| <a id="fn-codeUnits"></a>`codeUnits` | `codeUnits(text)` | `sum(codeUnits(tag)) % 8 → a stable color index for tag` |\n| <a id="fn-join"></a>`join` | `join(list, separator, field or item => value)` | `join(tags, " · ")` |\n| <a id="fn-pad"></a>`pad` | `pad(value, width, fill)` | `pad(5, 2) → 05` |\n| <a id="fn-text"></a>`text` | `text(value)` | `text(42) → "42"` |\n| <a id="fn-runs"></a>`runs` | `runs(list, item => condition)` | `runs(steps, s => s.h <= 1) → [{first, last, items, count}]` |\n| <a id="fn-interpolate"></a>`interpolate` | `interpolate(points, xField, yField, x)` | `interpolate(tides, "t", "v", now())` |\n\n(Continues: state.md#state-formula-functions.)'),
      DocSection('state-text', 'Text', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-left"></a>`left` | `left(text, count)` | `left("MX4821", 2) → MX` |\n| <a id="fn-right"></a>`right` | `right(text, count)` | `right("1FUJGLDR5MX4821", 6) → MX4821` |\n| <a id="fn-upper"></a>`upper` | `upper(text)` | `upper("hi") → HI` |\n| <a id="fn-lower"></a>`lower` | `lower(text)` | `lower("Hi") → hi` |\n| <a id="fn-trim"></a>`trim` | `trim(text)` | `trim("  hi ") → hi` |\n| <a id="fn-contains"></a>`contains` | `contains(text or list, value)` | `contains(lower(title), lower(search)) → true` |\n| <a id="fn-startsWith"></a>`startsWith` | `startsWith(text, prefix)` | `startsWith("Buy milk", "Buy") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-endsWith"></a>`endsWith` | `endsWith(text, suffix)` | `endsWith("photo.png", ".png") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-padLeft"></a>`padLeft` | `padLeft(value, width, char)` | `padLeft(4, 2) → 04 (numbers pad with 0, text with spaces)` |\n| `padLeft` | `padLeft(text, width, char?)` | `padLeft(42, 5, "0") → 00042` |\n| <a id="fn-padRight"></a>`padRight` | `padRight(value, width, char)` | `padRight("A", 3, ".") → A..` |\n| `padRight` | `padRight(text, width, char?)` | `padRight("ab", 4, ".") → ab..` |\n| <a id="fn-substring"></a>`substring` | `substring(text, start, end)` | `substring("Vinyl", 0, 3) → Vin` |\n| `substring` | `substring(text, start, end?)` | `substring("EX-102", 3) → 102` |\n| <a id="fn-replace"></a>`replace` | `replace(text, from, to)` | `replace("a-b-c", "-", " ") → a b c` |\n| `replace` | `replace(text, from, to)` | `replace("1,402", ",", "") → 1402` |\n| <a id="fn-regexReplace"></a>`regexReplace` | `regexReplace(text, pattern, to)` | `regexReplace("WILLOW PHARMACY 044", " [0-9]+\$", "") → WILLOW PHARMACY; \\\$1 in to inserts a group` |\n| <a id="fn-titleCase"></a>`titleCase` | `titleCase(text)` | `titleCase("SQ *KESTREL FLOWERS") → Sq *Kestrel Flowers` |\n| <a id="fn-split"></a>`split` | `split(text, separator)` | `split("rock, jazz", ", ") → [rock, jazz]` |\n| `split` | `split(text, separator?)` | `split("2481") → [2, 4, 8, 1]` |\n| <a id="fn-matches"></a>`matches` | `matches(text, pattern)` | `matches(code, "^\\d{4}\$") → true` |\n| <a id="fn-slug"></a>`slug` | `slug(text)` | `slug("Kind of Blue!") → kind-of-blue` |\n| <a id="fn-charCode"></a>`charCode` | `charCode(text, index)` | `charCode("MX", 1) → 88` |\n| <a id="fn-fromCharCode"></a>`fromCharCode` | `fromCharCode(code, …) or fromCharCode(list)` | `fromCharCode(65 + seat) → B` |\n| <a id="fn-codeUnits"></a>`codeUnits` | `codeUnits(text)` | `sum(codeUnits(tag)) % 8 → a stable color index for tag` |\n| <a id="fn-join"></a>`join` | `join(list, separator, field or item => value)` | `join(tags, " · ")` |\n| <a id="fn-pad"></a>`pad` | `pad(value, width, fill)` | `pad(5, 2) → 05` |\n| <a id="fn-text"></a>`text` | `text(value)` | `text(42) → "42"` |\n| <a id="fn-runs"></a>`runs` | `runs(list, item => condition)` | `runs(steps, s => s.h <= 1) → [{first, last, items, count}]` |\n| <a id="fn-interpolate"></a>`interpolate` | `interpolate(points, xField, yField, x)` | `interpolate(tides, "t", "v", now())` |\n| <a id="fn-textDirection"></a>`textDirection` | `textDirection(locale)` | `textDirection("he_IL") → rtl · textDirection("fr") → ltr` |\n\n(Continues: state.md#state-text.)'),
      DocSection('state-numbers-and-math', 'Numbers and math', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-round"></a>`round` | `round(value, decimals)` | `round(4.567, 1) → 4.6` |\n| <a id="fn-floor"></a>`floor` | `floor(value)` | `floor(4.7) → 4` |\n| <a id="fn-ceil"></a>`ceil` | `ceil(value)` | `ceil(4.2) → 5` |\n| <a id="fn-abs"></a>`abs` | `abs(value)` | `abs(-3) → 3` |\n| <a id="fn-min"></a>`min` | `min(a, b, …) or min(list)` | `min(3, 7) → 3` |\n| <a id="fn-max"></a>`max` | `max(a, b, …) or max(list)` | `max(3, 7) → 7` |\n| <a id="fn-sqrt"></a>`sqrt` | `sqrt(value)` | `sqrt(16) → 4` |\n| <a id="fn-pow"></a>`pow` | `pow(base, exponent)` | `pow(2, 10) → 1024` |\n| <a id="fn-exp"></a>`exp` | `exp(value)` | `exp(1) → 2.71828… (zoom by exp(-delta / 500))` |\n| <a id="fn-ln"></a>`ln` | `ln(value)` | `ln(exp(2)) → 2` |\n| <a id="fn-log"></a>`log` | `log(value, base?)` | `log(1000) → 3, log(8, 2) → 3` |\n| <a id="fn-sign"></a>`sign` | `sign(value)` | `sign(-4) → -1` |\n| <a id="fn-hypot"></a>`hypot` | `hypot(x, y)` | `hypot(3, 4) → 5` |\n| <a id="fn-sin"></a>`sin` | `sin(radians)` | `sin(pi() / 2) → 1` |\n| <a id="fn-cos"></a>`cos` | `cos(radians)` | `cos(0) → 1` |\n| <a id="fn-tan"></a>`tan` | `tan(radians)` | `tan(0) → 0` |\n| <a id="fn-asin"></a>`asin` | `asin(value)` | `asin(1) → 1.5708` |\n| <a id="fn-acos"></a>`acos` | `acos(value)` | `acos(1) → 0` |\n| <a id="fn-atan"></a>`atan` | `atan(value)` | `atan(1) → 0.7854` |\n| <a id="fn-atan2"></a>`atan2` | `atan2(y, x)` | `atan2(1, 1) → 0.7854` |\n| <a id="fn-pi"></a>`pi` | `pi or pi()` | `pi → 3.14159…` |\n| <a id="fn-radians"></a>`radians` | `radians(degrees)` | `radians(180) → 3.14159…` |\n| <a id="fn-degrees"></a>`degrees` | `degrees(radians)` | `degrees(pi()) → 180` |\n| <a id="fn-clamp"></a>`clamp` | `clamp(value, min, max)` | `clamp(12, 0, 10) → 10` |\n| <a id="fn-distance"></a>`distance` | `distance(lat1, lng1, lat2, lng2, \'km\' or \'mi\')` | `distance(a.lat, a.lng, b.lat, b.lng, \'mi\') → 362.4` |\n| <a id="fn-number"></a>`number` | `number(value)` | `number("42") → 42` |\n| <a id="fn-random"></a>`random` | `random() · random(n) · random(a, b)` | `random(1, 6) → a whole number from 1 to 6` |\n| <a id="fn-fill"></a>`fill` | `fill(template, map or list)` | `fill("{i} of {n}", {i: 1, n: 10}) → 1 of 10` |\n| <a id="fn-fixed"></a>`fixed` | `fixed(value, decimals)` | `fixed(4.5, 2) → 4.50` |\n| <a id="fn-feetInches"></a>`feetInches` | `feetInches(feet)` | `feetInches(6.67) → 6′ 8″` |\n| <a id="fn-thousands"></a>`thousands` | `thousands(value, decimals)` | `thousands(1094) → 1,094` |\n| <a id="fn-seconds"></a>`seconds` | `seconds("m:ss" or "h:mm:ss")` | `seconds("3:45") → 225` |\n| <a id="fn-duration"></a>`duration` | `duration(seconds)` | `duration(225) → 3:45` |'),
      DocSection('state-money-and-number-formatting', 'Money and number formatting', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-money"></a>`money` | `money(value, symbol, decimals) or money(value, decimals)` | `money(price) → \$1,234.50` |\n| <a id="fn-currency"></a>`currency` | `currency(value, code, options?)` | `currency(-1234.5, "EUR") → −1.234,50 €; currency(42, "USD", "signed") → +\$42.00` |\n| <a id="fn-parseAmount"></a>`parseAmount` | `parseAmount(text, code)` | `parseAmount("1.234,50", "EUR") → 1234.5` |\n| <a id="fn-formatAmount"></a>`formatAmount` | `formatAmount(text, code)` | `formatAmount("12345.6", "USD") → 12,345.6` |\n| <a id="fn-currencySymbol"></a>`currencySymbol` | `currencySymbol(code)` | `currencySymbol("GBP") → £` |\n| <a id="fn-currencyDecimals"></a>`currencyDecimals` | `currencyDecimals(code)` | `currencyDecimals("JPY") → 0` |\n| <a id="fn-formatNumber"></a>`formatNumber` | `formatNumber(value, digits?, locale?)` | `formatNumber(2481.64, 1) → 2,481.6 · formatNumber(1234.5, 1, "ar_EG") → ١٬٢٣٤٫٥` |\n| <a id="fn-formatCurrency"></a>`formatCurrency` | `formatCurrency(value, currencyCode, locale?, decimals?)` | `formatCurrency(1234.5, "EUR", "fr_FR") → 1 234,50 € · formatCurrency(1500, "JPY", "ja_JP") → ￥1,500` |\n| <a id="fn-formatPercent"></a>`formatPercent` | `formatPercent(value, locale?, decimals?)` | `formatPercent(0.42) → 42% · formatPercent(0.42, "fr_FR") → 42 %` |'),
      DocSection('state-lists', 'Lists', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-sum"></a>`sum` | `sum(list, field or item => value)` | `sum(cart, i => i.price * i.qty) → 24` |\n| <a id="fn-count"></a>`count` | `count(list, item => condition) or count(list, field, value)` | `count(tasks, t => !t.done) → 2` |\n| <a id="fn-length"></a>`length` | `length(text or list)` | `length(cart) → 3` |\n| <a id="fn-filter"></a>`filter` | `filter(list, item => condition) or filter(list, field, value)` | `filter(tasks, t => contains(lower(t.title), lower(search)))` |\n| <a id="fn-where"></a>`where` | `where(list, field, value) or where(list, item => condition)` | `where(tasks, "done", false)` |\n| <a id="fn-find"></a>`find` | `find(list, item => condition) or find(list, field, value)` | `find(users, u => u.id == userId)` |\n| <a id="fn-any"></a>`any` | `any(list, item => condition) or any(list, field, value)` | `any(tasks, t => t.due < today()) → true` |\n| <a id="fn-all"></a>`all` | `all(list, item => condition) or all(list, field, value)` | `all(tasks, "done") → false` |\n| <a id="fn-map"></a>`map` | `map(list, field or item => value or (item, index) => value)` | `map(cart, i => i.price * i.qty) → [8, 16]` |\n| <a id="fn-sortBy"></a>`sortBy` | `sortBy(list, field or item => key, "desc", more keys…)` | `sortBy(records, r => r.artist, r => r.year, "desc") (missing keys last)` |\n| <a id="fn-sortByDesc"></a>`sortByDesc` | `sortByDesc(list, field or item => key, more keys…)` | `sortByDesc(records, "year")` |\n| <a id="fn-findIndex"></a>`findIndex` | `findIndex(list, item => condition) or findIndex(list, field, value)` | `findIndex(records, r => r.id == selectedId) → 2 (-1 when none)` |\n| `findIndex` | `findIndex(list, item => condition) or findIndex(list, field, value)` | `findIndex(tasks, "id", id) → 2 (-1 when missing)` |\n| <a id="fn-groupBy"></a>`groupBy` | `groupBy(list, field or item => key) → [{key, items, count}]` | `groupBy(txns, "date") → one entry per day, in order of first appearance` |\n| <a id="fn-unique"></a>`unique` | `unique(list, field or item => key)` | `unique(tags) or unique(tasks, "category")` |\n| <a id="fn-without"></a>`without` | `without(list, other or item) or without(map, keys)` | `without(held, 64) or without(task, ["draft", "tmp"])` |\n| <a id="fn-concat"></a>`concat` | `concat(list or item, ...)` | `concat([record.art], sleeves) or list1 + list2` |\n| `concat` | `concat(list, list2, ...)` | `concat(range(2), [9]) → [0, 1, 9]` |\n| <a id="fn-first"></a>`first` | `first(list)` | `first(stops) → the first stop` |\n| <a id="fn-last"></a>`last` | `last(list)` | `last(stops) → the last stop` |\n| <a id="fn-slice"></a>`slice` | `slice(list, start, end)` | `slice([\'a\', \'b\', \'c\', \'d\'], 1, 3) → [\'b\', \'c\']` |\n| <a id="fn-take"></a>`take` | `take(list, n)` | `take(stops, index) → stops before this one` |\n| `take` | `take(list, count)` | `take(pareto, index + 1)` |\n| <a id="fn-skip"></a>`skip` | `skip(list, n)` | `skip(stops, 1) → all but the first` |\n| `skip` | `skip(list, count)` | `skip(events, 25)` |\n| <a id="fn-reverse"></a>`reverse` | `reverse(list or text)` | `reverse([1, 2, 3]) → [3, 2, 1]` |\n\n(Continues: state.md#state-lists.)'),
      DocSection('state-objects', 'Objects', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-object"></a>`object` | `object(key, value, key, value, …)` | `object(\'nights\', 2, \'cg\', id) → {nights: 2, cg: id}` |\n| <a id="fn-obj"></a>`obj` | `obj(key, value, key2, value2, ...)` | `obj("id", "ex1", "hours", 12) → {id: ex1, hours: 12}` |\n| <a id="fn-merge"></a>`merge` | `merge(map, map, …)` | `merge(stop, object(\'nights\', 3)) → stop with 3 nights` |\n| <a id="fn-set"></a>`set` | `set(map, key, value, …) or set(list, index, value)` | `set(rig, \'length\', 36) → rig, 36 ft long` |\n| <a id="fn-keys"></a>`keys` | `keys(map)` | `keys(rig) → [name, length, …]` |\n| <a id="fn-values"></a>`values` | `values(map)` | `values(totals) → [3, 5]` |\n| <a id="fn-get"></a>`get` | `get(map or list, key)` | `get(lineNames, item.line) → \'Weld\'` |\n| <a id="fn-unset"></a>`unset` | `unset(map, key)` | `unset(task, "draft")` |\n| <a id="fn-with"></a>`with` | `with(map, key, value, …)` | `with(item, \'x\', item.x + 1) → item with x changed` |\n| <a id="fn-newId"></a>`newId` | `newId(prefix)` | `newId("task") → task_k3x9f2` |'),
      DocSection('state-dates-and-time', 'Dates and time', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-now"></a>`now` | `now(utcOffset?)` | `now() → 2026-10-21T14:30:00.000, now("-07:00") at UTC−7` |\n| <a id="fn-nowMs"></a>`nowMs` | `nowMs()` | `nowMs() → 1793356053036, milliseconds since 1970 (time taps: 60000 / (nowMs() - lastTap) is a tempo)` |\n| <a id="fn-today"></a>`today` | `today(utcOffset?)` | `today() → 2026-10-21T00:00:00.000` |\n| <a id="fn-wallTime"></a>`wallTime` | `wallTime(dateWithOffset)` | `wallTime("2026-10-22T07:25:17-07:00") → 2026-10-22T07:25:17.000` |\n| <a id="fn-parseDate"></a>`parseDate` | `parseDate(text or millis)` | `parseDate("10/21/2026") or parseDate("Oct 21, 2026") → 2026-10-21; null when not a real date` |\n| <a id="fn-formatDate"></a>`formatDate` | `formatDate(date, pattern or style, locale?)` | `formatDate(now(), "EEE, MMM d · h:mm a") → Wed, Oct 21 · 2:30 PM · formatDate(today(), "full", "fr_FR") → jeudi 30 octobre 2026` |\n| <a id="fn-addSeconds"></a>`addSeconds` | `addSeconds(date, seconds)` | `addSeconds(start, 90)` |\n| <a id="fn-diffSeconds"></a>`diffSeconds` | `diffSeconds(from, to)` | `diffSeconds(startedAt, now()) → 240` |\n| <a id="fn-formatDuration"></a>`formatDuration` | `formatDuration(seconds, pattern)` | `formatDuration(6480, \'h:mm:ss\') → 1:48:00 · \'mm:ss\' → 108:00 · \'compact\' → 1h 48m` |\n| <a id="fn-addMinutes"></a>`addMinutes` | `addMinutes(date, minutes)` | `addMinutes(start, 90)` |\n| <a id="fn-addHours"></a>`addHours` | `addHours(date, hours)` | `addHours(now(), 2)` |\n| <a id="fn-addDays"></a>`addDays` | `addDays(date, days)` | `addDays(today(), 7)` |\n| <a id="fn-addMonths"></a>`addMonths` | `addMonths(date, months)` | `addMonths("2026-01-31", 1) → 2026-02-28T00:00:00.000` |\n| <a id="fn-diffMinutes"></a>`diffMinutes` | `diffMinutes(from, to)` | `diffMinutes(start, end) → 45` |\n| <a id="fn-diffHours"></a>`diffHours` | `diffHours(from, to)` | `diffHours(start, end) → 3` |\n| <a id="fn-diffDays"></a>`diffDays` | `diffDays(from, to)` | `diffDays(today(), dueDate) → 5` |\n| <a id="fn-timeAgo"></a>`timeAgo` | `timeAgo(date, style?, locale?, labels?)` | `timeAgo(sentAt) → now · 5m · 3h · Yesterday · 3d · Mar 4 · timeAgo(sentAt, "long") → 5 minutes ago (alias formatRelative)` |\n| <a id="fn-formatRelative"></a>`formatRelative` | `formatRelative(date, style?, locale?, labels?)` | `formatRelative(sentAt) → 3h (the same as timeAgo)` |\n| <a id="fn-isToday"></a>`isToday` | `isToday(date)` | `isToday(sentAt) → true` |\n| <a id="fn-isPast"></a>`isPast` | `isPast(date)` | `isPast(expiresAt) → true once it has passed (checked every minute)` |\n| <a id="fn-isFuture"></a>`isFuture` | `isFuture(date)` | `isFuture(startsAt) → true until it comes (checked every minute)` |\n| <a id="fn-isSameDay"></a>`isSameDay` | `isSameDay(a, b)` | `isSameDay(a.sentAt, b.sentAt) → false` |\n| <a id="fn-isBefore"></a>`isBefore` | `isBefore(a, b)` | `isBefore(expiresAt, now()) → true` |\n| <a id="fn-isAfter"></a>`isAfter` | `isAfter(a, b)` | `isAfter(startsAt, now()) → false` |\n| <a id="fn-year"></a>`year` | `year(date)` | `year("2026-10-21") → 2026` |\n| <a id="fn-month"></a>`month` | `month(date)` | `month("2026-10-21") → 10` |\n\n(Continues: state.md#state-dates-and-time.)'),
      DocSection('state-colors', 'Colors', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-luminance"></a>`luminance` | `luminance(color)` | `luminance("#FFFFFF") → 1` |\n| <a id="fn-mix"></a>`mix` | `mix(color1, color2, amount)` | `mix(\'#FFFFFF\', \'#000000\', 0.25) → #BFBFBF` |\n| `mix` | `mix(colorA, colorB, t)` | `mix(\'#000000\', \'#FFFFFF\', 0.5) → #FF808080` |\n| <a id="fn-alpha"></a>`alpha` | `alpha(color, opacity)` | `alpha(\'#FF4D4F\', 0.12) → #1FFF4D4F` |\n| <a id="fn-lerpColor"></a>`lerpColor` | `lerpColor(colorA, colorB, t), same as mix` | `lerpColor(\'#FF4D4F\', \'#1677FF\', 0.25) → #FFC5587B` |'),
      DocSection('state-logic', 'Logic', '| Function | Signature | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| <a id="fn-if"></a>`if` | `if(condition, then, else)` | `if(qty > 1, "items", "item")` |\n| <a id="fn-coalesce"></a>`coalesce` | `coalesce(value, fallback, ...)` | `coalesce(route.date, today())` |'),
      DocSection('state-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-valueChanged"></a>`valueChanged` | Variable `Trigger.variable` changed while the screen shows. |\n| <a id="trigger-actionError"></a>`actionError` | On the current canvas: a failed action chain or cloud subscription. `\${result.error}` is `{type, message, action, nodeId}` (no stack or raw service objects). A failure in this reaction reports to the host without recursively firing another actionError reaction. |'),
      DocSection('state-computed-and-function-variables', 'Computed and function variables', 'A variable with a `formula` (what goes in `\${= ...}`) is read-only and follows what it reads; with `parameters` it\nis a function any formula calls by name. Declare them in `page_variables` to share them with every canvas of the\ndocument:\n\n```json\n"variables": {"page_variables": [\n  {"name": "query", "type": "text", "value": ""},\n  {"name": "dishes", "type": "list", "value": [{"name": "Lamb", "vegan": false}, {"name": "Squash", "vegan": true}]},\n  {"name": "shown", "type": "list", "formula": "filter(dishes, d => contains(lower(d.name), lower(query)))"},\n  {"name": "shownCount", "type": "integer", "formula": "length(shown)"},\n  {"name": "usd", "type": "text", "parameters": ["n"], "formula": "\'\$\' + round(n)"}\n]}\n```\n\n`\${shown}` feeds a list, `\${shownCount}` a label, `\${= usd(price * 12)}` any text: write a filter or a rule once,\nnot in every binding. A function variable\'s name must not be a formula function\'s (the built-in one wins).'),
      DocSection('state-a-streak-and-other-counts-from-data', 'A streak and other counts from data', 'Derive, do not store: a computed variable over the records. Habits done today: `count(habits, h => h.done)`.\nTotals: `sum(map(cart, i => i.price * i.qty))`. Dates: `formatDate(today(), \'EEE d\')`, `addDays(today(), -i)`,\n`weekday(date)` (Monday is 1). Function variables may call each other. A streak (checked days in a row ending at\nday `end` of a list of booleans): the days up to `end`, reversed, and the index of the first unchecked one.\n\n```json\n"variables": {"page_variables": [\n  {"name": "todayIdx", "type": "integer", "formula": "weekday(today()) - 1"},\n  {"name": "gapAt", "type": "integer", "parameters": ["days", "end"], "formula": "findIndex(reverse(take(days, end + 1)), d => !d)"},\n  {"name": "streak", "type": "integer", "parameters": ["days", "end"], "formula": "gapAt(days, end) < 0 ? end + 1 : gapAt(days, end)"}\n]}\n```\n\n`\${= streak(item.days, todayIdx)}` in a habit\'s row; `\${= streak(item.days, todayIdx - 1)}` when today is not\nchecked yet. For anything with a real loop, a script.'),
      DocSection('state-changing-state-from-a-reaction', 'Changing state from a reaction', '`setVariable` with `op`: `set` (default), `toggle`, `add` (a number adds; a list appends; a map merges),\n`subtract`, `insert` / `removeAt` / `update` at `index`, `remove`. `value` is an expression. A chain that branches:\n`if` with a `condition` (a predicate: `{"left": "\${count}", "op": "greaterThan", "right": "5"}`, `{"left":\n"\${name}", "op": "isEmpty"}`; every op is in [Conditions](#state-conditions)) and `then` / `else` chains. Every\naction also takes `when`, the same kind of predicate object (run only while it holds); a trigger\'s `when` is a\nformula string instead (`"when": "!item.future"`). `forEach` runs a chain per item; `delay` waits.\n\n```json\n{"type": "if", "condition": {"left": "\${= contains(saved, trip.id)}", "op": "isTrue"},\n "then": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "saved", "op": "remove", "value": "\${trip.id}"}],\n "else": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "saved", "op": "add", "value": "\${trip.id}"}]}\n```\n\nThe condition is an object, never a formula string: a formula goes in `left` with `"op": "isTrue"`.'),
      DocSection('state-setting-several-nodes-with-a-condition', 'Setting several nodes with a condition', 'A condition sets node fields while a test holds: an ordered list of branches (if, else if, ..., else) under a canvas\nid in the document\'s `conditions`. For one field the first branch that holds and sets it wins; a condition wins\nover the node\'s binding. A binding with a formula is often simpler; conditions suit setting several nodes at once.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["plans"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "plans": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 300},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["toggle", "price", "note"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 300}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12, "crossAxisAlignment": "start"}\n    },\n    "toggle": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["toggleLabel"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"hug": 36}, "padding": [14, 8, 14, 8]},\n      "decoration": {"strokes": [{"color": "#FF2563EB"}], "radius": 18},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "annual", "op": "toggle"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "toggleLabel": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 80}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "Monthly", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF2563EB"}},\n      "bind": {"props.text": "\${= annual ? \'Annual billing\' : \'Monthly billing\'}"}\n    },\n    "price": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 80}, "height": {"hug": 40}},\n      "props": {"text": "\$12 / month", "style": {"fontSize": 32, "fontWeight": 700, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "note": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 80}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "Save 20% with annual billing", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF16A34A"}}\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {"plans": [{"name": "annual", "type": "boolean", "value": false}]},\n  "conditions": {\n    "plans": [\n      {\n        "id": "billing",\n        "branches": [\n          {\n            "when": {"left": "\${annual}", "op": "isTrue"},\n            "set": [\n              {"node": "price", "path": "props.text", "value": "\$120 / year"},\n              {"node": "note", "path": "visible", "value": false}\n            ]\n          },\n          {"set": [{"node": "price", "path": "props.text", "value": "\$12 / month"}]}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```'),
      DocSection('state-when-to-use-a-script', 'When to use a script', 'For multi-step state changes (a puzzle\'s checks, a game step, a streak over dates), a script reads and sets\nvariables with `vars.get(name)` and `vars.set(name, value)` (capabilities `variables.read`, `variables.write`);\nthe UI updates through what binds to them. A script cannot draw or touch nodes. A reaction runs it (`{"type":\n"runScript", "script": "place", "arguments": {"cell": "\${index}"}}`); a formula calls a pure one\n(`\${= script.isSolved(board)}`).'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'interaction',
    title: 'Interaction: reactions, states and gestures',
    summary: 'What a node does when it is tapped, hovered, pressed, dragged or swiped: reactions and every trigger, hover and pressed styles (`states`), ink ripples, tooltips, letting taps through, drag and drop, values set by dragging (`track`), swipe to dismiss, pan, pinch and rotate, keys, the clipboard and haptics.',
    when: 'What a node does when it is tapped, hovered, pressed, dragged or swiped: reactions and every trigger, hover and\npressed styles (`states`), ink ripples, tooltips, letting taps through, drag and drop, values set by dragging\n(`track`), swipe to dismiss, pan, pinch and rotate, keys, the clipboard and haptics.',
    example: 'A button-like row that changes colour while hovered and pressed, and while selected:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["buttons"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "buttons": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["cta"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 200}},\n      "props": {"mainAxisAlignment": "center"}\n    },\n    "cta": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["ctaLabel"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 160}, "height": {"hug": 44}, "padding": [20, 12, 20, 12]},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF2563EB"}], "radius": 10},\n      "states": {\n        "hovered": {\n          "cta": {"decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF1D4ED8"}]}},\n          "ctaLabel": {"props": {"text": "Let\'s go"}}\n        },\n        "pressed": {"cta": {"opacity": 0.8}}\n      },\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "openLink", "url": "https://example.com"}]}]\n    },\n    "ctaLabel": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 100}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "Get started", "style": {"fontSize": 16, "fontWeight": 600, "color": "#FFFFFFFF"}}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- `hovered` never happens on touch screens.\n- The innermost tappable node takes the tap; `ignorePointer` lets it through.\n- A state patch names node ids inside the node; patching a node outside it does nothing.\n- An interaction state\'s patch loses to a binding of the same field (bindings come after states).\n- A misspelled trigger is `unknown_trigger`; a key it does not take is `unknown_trigger_key`.\n- `tap_no_reaction` (render command): a `--tap` step hit a node with no reaction.',
    words: 5162,
    items: ['states', 'inkWell', 'tooltip', 'ignorePointer', 'draggable', 'dropTarget', 'track', 'dismissible', 'pan', 'transformGesture', 'click', 'doubleTap', 'longPress', 'hold', 'secondaryClick', 'pointerDown', 'pointerUp', 'hover', 'cursorEnter', 'cursorExit', 'swipeLeft', 'swipeRight', 'swipeUp', 'swipeDown', 'drag', 'dragEnd', 'wheel', 'pinch', 'dragStart', 'dragCancel', 'dragCompleted', 'drop', 'dragEnter', 'dragExit', 'dropRejected', 'controlTrack', 'controlDismissible', 'controlTransform', 'copyToClipboard', 'haptic'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('interaction-trigger-fields', 'Trigger fields', 'A trigger is `{"type": "<type>", ...these}`, or just the type as a string (`"click"`).\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `type` | [TriggerType](values.md#enum-TriggerType) | `"click"` |  |  |\n| `debounceMs` | int | `0` |  | Waits this long after the last trigger before running, so a burst (typing in a search field) runs once. 0 runs every time. |\n| `variable` | String | `""` |  | `TriggerType.valueChanged`: the variable watched. |\n| `intervalMs` | int | `1000` |  | Timer: ms between ticks (a number or an expression). |\n| `key` | String | `""` |  | Key triggers: the key or combination (`KeyCombo`); empty: any key. |\n| `when` | String | `""` |  | A formula; the reaction runs only while it\'s true (key triggers take the key only then; a timer or a frame ticker runs only then). Empty: always. |\n| `holdMs` | int | `1200` |  | `TriggerType.hold`: how long the press is held. |\n| `visibleFraction` | double | `0.15` |  | Viewport triggers: the visible share (0–1) that counts as in view. |\n| `repeat` | bool | `false` |  | keyDown: also while the key repeats. |\n| `visibleMs` | int | `0` | ≥ 0 | Viewport: how long it stays in view before firing (ms). |\n| `onceKey` | String | `""` |  | Runs once per key (an expression, such as \${item.id}) per app session. |\n| `event` | String | `""` |  | event: the key of the component event it handles (one of the component\'s widget.events). |'),
      DocSection('interaction-fields-every-action-has', 'Fields every action has', '| Key | Type | Default | Allowed | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `enabled` | bool | `true` |  | False skips the action. |\n| `nonBlocking` | bool | `false` |  | The chain doesn\'t wait for it, and its failure doesn\'t stop the chain. |\n| `when` | Object | unset |  | Runs only when it holds. |\n\nFields holding nested action chains (a list of actions): `then`, `else`, `actions`, `onSuccess`, `onError`, `cancelActions`.'),
      DocSection('interaction-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-click"></a>`click` | A tap (a click with a mouse). `\${result}` holds where it landed (`x`, `y` in the node, `globalX`, `globalY`) and the modifier keys held (`meta`, `shift`, `alt`). |\n| <a id="trigger-doubleTap"></a>`doubleTap` | Two taps in quick succession. A node with double tap reactions waits out the double tap timeout before its single taps run. |\n| <a id="trigger-longPress"></a>`longPress` | A long press. |\n| <a id="trigger-hold"></a>`hold` | A press held for `Trigger.holdMs`; letting go early cancels it. |\n| <a id="trigger-secondaryClick"></a>`secondaryClick` | A right click, or a two-finger tap on a trackpad (`\${result.x}`, `\${result.y}`: where, on screen). |\n| <a id="trigger-pointerDown"></a>`pointerDown` | A pointer went down on the node. |\n| <a id="trigger-pointerUp"></a>`pointerUp` | A pointer went up (or was canceled) on the node. |\n| <a id="trigger-hover"></a>`hover` | The mouse cursor moved over the node (fires when it enters, too). |\n| <a id="trigger-cursorEnter"></a>`cursorEnter` | The mouse cursor entered the node (once). |\n| <a id="trigger-cursorExit"></a>`cursorExit` | The mouse cursor left the node (once). |\n| <a id="trigger-swipeLeft"></a>`swipeLeft` | A swipe (a fling) to the left, right, up or down. |\n| <a id="trigger-swipeRight"></a>`swipeRight` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-swipeUp"></a>`swipeUp` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-swipeDown"></a>`swipeDown` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-drag"></a>`drag` | The node is dragged (every move); `dragEnd` when it\'s let go. |\n| <a id="trigger-dragEnd"></a>`dragEnd` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-wheel"></a>`wheel` | Wheel or trackpad scroll over the node; a pinch on it. |\n| <a id="trigger-pinch"></a>`pinch` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-dragStart"></a>`dragStart` | Drag and drop: on a draggable (start, cancel, completed) and on a drop target (drop, enter, exit, rejected). `\${result}` and `\${drag}` hold the drag. A list with a `reorder` fires `dragStart` when a row is picked up and `dragCompleted` when it is let go (moved or not), with `\${result.index}` and `\${result.item}`: a list can change while a row is lifted (fold its rows into tiles). On a node with a `drag` reaction (and no drag and drop), `dragStart` is the start of that one-finger drag, where the finger went down (`\${drag.x}`, `\${drag.y}`): begin a stroke there rather than on `pointerDown`, which fires for every finger of a pinch. |\n| <a id="trigger-dragCancel"></a>`dragCancel` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-dragCompleted"></a>`dragCompleted` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-drop"></a>`drop` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-dragEnter"></a>`dragEnter` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-dragExit"></a>`dragExit` |  |\n| <a id="trigger-dropRejected"></a>`dropRejected` |  |'),
      DocSection('interaction-reactions', 'Reactions', 'A node\'s `actions` is a list of **reactions**: a trigger and the chain of actions it runs, in order.\n\n- In a chain `\${result}` starts as the trigger\'s event (where a click landed; a text field\'s text; a checkbox\'s\n  value) and is replaced only by an action that gives a value (`callApi`, `openModal`\'s closing value, `runScript`,\n  `callFunction`, a cloud read); `setVariable`, `navigate`, `showToast`, `scrollTo` leave it as it was.\n- A tap on a control (a checkbox, a switch, a button, a text field) inside a node with a `click` reaction runs the\n  control\'s reaction only, as Flutter\'s gesture arena gives the tap to the innermost recognizer. To toggle from the\n  whole row with one handler, give the control `"ignorePointer": true` and bind its value.\n- Screen triggers (`load`, `valueChanged`, `timer`, `frame`, `keyDown`) go on the canvas.\n- Every action also takes `enabled`, `nonBlocking` and `when` (run only while a predicate holds:\n  `{"left": "\${count}", "op": "greaterThan", "right": "5"}`; the ops are in [Conditions](state.md#state-conditions)). A\n  trigger\'s own `when` is a formula string.\n- Write each action\'s fields flat in the action object; a misspelled key is dropped by the runtime and reported by\n  validation (`unknown_action_key`).'),
      DocSection('interaction-hover-press-and-other-states', 'Hover, press and other states', '`states` on a node changes it and its descendants while it is `hovered`, `pressed`, `focused`, `selected`,\n`disabled` or `dragged`. Each state maps node ids (the node itself or nodes inside it) to a **patch**: partial node\nJSON merged over that node (objects merge, other values replace, `null` removes). `selected` and `disabled` follow\nbindings: `"bind": {"selected": "\${= tab == \'pricing\'}"}` puts the node in its `selected` state. `hovered` needs a\nmouse: on touch screens it never happens, so do not hide anything behind it. Animate the change with\n`transitions` ([animation](animation.md#page-animation)).'),
      DocSection('interaction-a-segmented-toggle-monthly-annual', 'A segmented toggle (monthly / annual)', 'Two labels in a row with a fill; each label\'s `selected` binds to the variable (`\${= annual}` and\n`\${= !annual}`), its `states.selected` patches its fill and text colour, and its click sets the variable. A\n`switch` bound two-way to the same variable works as well.'),
      DocSection('interaction-drag-and-drop', 'Drag and drop', '`draggable` (`{"group": "card", "data": "\${item.id}"}`) lets the node be picked up; a `dropTarget` that `accepts`\nthe group takes it, and its `drop` reaction reads the data as `\${result}`. Reordering a list: the list\'s `reorder`\nsettings with a `reorderHandle` in the item, and the `reorder` trigger.'),
      DocSection('interaction-values-set-by-dragging-swiping-pinching', 'Values set by dragging, swiping, pinching', '`track` sets a variable as the pointer moves along a line, arc or path (a custom slider, a dial). `dismissible`\nswipes a node away (a list item; the `swipeAction` trigger). `pan` makes a node follow the pointer;\n`transformGesture` pinches, pans and rotates with fling physics. The `drag` trigger reports `\${result.dx}`,\n`\${result.dy}` per move and `dragEnd` the velocity, for game controls.'),
      DocSection('interaction-copy-to-the-clipboard', 'Copy to the clipboard', '`{"type": "copyToClipboard", "text": "\${address}"}` (the key is `text`), then the chain goes on: a toast or a\n"Copied" state after it. The render command copies in memory and lists what was copied in its report.'),
      DocSection('interaction-keys', 'Keys', 'A canvas\'s `keyDown` reaction (`{"trigger": {"type": "keyDown", "key": "ArrowRight"}, ...}`) runs while no text\nfield has the focus: arrow keys between tabs are two reactions that set the tab variable\n(`\${= (tabIndex + 1) % 4}`), Escape closing a menu is one.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'animation',
    title: 'Animation and motion',
    summary: 'Anything that moves: a change that animates (implicit transitions), keyframe animations and presets, moving, scaling and turning a node without changing layout (`motion`), shared-element flights (`hero`), reveal on scroll, shimmer, typewriter text, particles, flip cards and tilt, and the timer and frame triggers for clocks and games.',
    when: 'Anything that moves: a change that animates (implicit transitions), keyframe animations and presets, moving,\nscaling and turning a node without changing layout (`motion`), shared-element flights (`hero`), reveal on\nscroll, shimmer, typewriter text, particles, flip cards and tilt, and the timer and frame triggers for clocks and\ngames.',
    example: 'A habit check-off: tapping the circle toggles `done`; its fill and scale change through bindings, and\n`transitions` animate the change (a small overshoot), while the label fades.\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["habit"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "habit": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "row"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "row": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["check", "label"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 120}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "check": {\n      "type": "box",\n      "layout": {"width": 32, "height": 32},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFE5E7EB"}], "radius": 16},\n      "bind": {\n        "decoration.fills[0].color": "\${= done ? \'#FF16A34A\' : \'#FFE5E7EB\'}",\n        "motion.scale": "\${= done ? 1.15 : 1}"\n      },\n      "transitions": [\n        {"property": "motion", "duration": 250, "curve": "easeOutBack"},\n        {"property": "decoration", "duration": 200}\n      ],\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "done", "op": "toggle"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "label": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 280}, "height": {"hug": 22}},\n      "props": {"text": "Drink water", "style": {"fontSize": 17, "color": "#FF111827"}},\n      "bind": {"opacity": "\${= done ? 0.5 : 1}"},\n      "transitions": [{"property": "opacity", "duration": 200}]\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {"habit": [{"name": "done", "type": "boolean", "value": false}]}\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- `motion` (its scale and rotate too) does not change layout: neighbours do not move. To make room, animate a\n  layout field.\n- A transition animates changes only; a value that never changes needs an animation that autoplays.\n- An animation\'s `id` is what `animate` names; without `autoplay` it waits.\n- Animations run in a running app. The render command settles about a second after each step, so a short\n  animation is over when it captures; to check one mid-flight, lengthen its duration in a copy.',
    words: 4610,
    items: ['motion', 'animations', 'transitions', 'shimmer', 'reveal', 'typewriter', 'particles', 'flip', 'tilt', 'hero', 'viewProgress', 'timer', 'frame', 'animate'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('animation-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-timer"></a>`timer` | Every `Trigger.intervalMs` while the screen shows (`Timer.periodic`) and `Trigger.when` holds; `\${result.tick}` counts. |\n| <a id="trigger-frame"></a>`frame` | Every frame while the node is on stage and `Trigger.when` holds (a `Ticker`): `\${result.dt}` (ms since the tick this chain last got), `\${result.elapsed}` (ms since it started), `\${result.frame}`. A frame that comes while the chain still runs is skipped; its time goes to the next `dt`. A design canvas never ticks. |'),
      DocSection('animation-animate-a-change-transitions', 'Animate a change (transitions)', '`transitions` is Flutter\'s implicit animation: when the value at a path changes (a binding, a condition, a state\npatch), the node tweens from what it shows to the new value. One entry per path or prefix: `{"property": "motion",\n"duration": 250, "curve": "easeOutBack"}`, `"opacity"`, `"decoration"`, `"layout.height"`; `"*"` for every path.\nThis is the simplest way to animate a check-off, a selected card or an opening panel.'),
      DocSection('animation-move-scale-or-turn-without-changing-layout-motion', 'Move, scale or turn without changing layout (motion)', '`motion` is a transform painted over the node\'s layout (Flutter\'s `Transform`): `translateX`/`translateY` in pixels,\n`scale`, `rotate` in degrees, 3D `rotateX`/`rotateY` with `perspective`, about `alignment` (the center by default).\nIt is the one way to scale or turn a node: there is no node `scale` and no `layout.rotation` (a turned node keeps\nits unturned box in the layout, as `Transform.rotate` does; Flutter\'s `RotatedBox` has no counterpart). Nothing else\nmoves. Bind a field (`"motion.rotate": "\${= open ? 180 : 0}"`) and add a transition to animate it; a transition on\n`motion.scale` times the scale apart from the rest of the motion (`AnimatedScale` beside `AnimatedSlide`).'),
      DocSection('animation-play-an-animation-animations-and-presets', 'Play an animation (animations and presets)', '`animations` holds a node\'s controllers: each runs 0 → 1 over `duration` (or a `spring`), after `delay`, once or\n`repeat`ed, and drives `tracks` of keyframes on its paths. A `preset` names a ready-made one (fade in, slide up,\npulse...) with its `params`. `autoplay` false waits for the `animate` action (`forward`, `reverse`, `stop`...) or a\nchange of `playKey`. A screen-wide animation sits on the canvas.'),
      DocSection('animation-reveal-on-scroll-view-progress-sticky-effects', 'Reveal on scroll, view progress, sticky effects', 'An entrance when a node scrolls into view (CSS scroll-reveal) is an **animation with `visibleFraction`**: it waits\nuntil that share of the node is in view, then plays.\n\n```json\n"animations": [{"id": "enter", "duration": 600, "curve": "easeOut", "visibleFraction": 0.3,\n                "tracks": [{"path": "opacity", "from": 0, "to": 1}, {"path": "motion.translateY", "from": 24, "to": 0}]}]\n```\n\nThe `reveal` behavior is not an entrance, despite its name: it **scrolls** the node into view (a chat\'s newest\nline). `viewProgress` gives `\${view.progress}` (0–1 through the viewport) to bind to, for effects that follow the\nscroll; the `enterViewport` and `exitViewport` triggers run actions. A page\'s reading progress:\n[scroll progress](layout.md#layout-scroll-progress).'),
      DocSection('animation-shared-elements-hero', 'Shared elements (hero)', '`hero` is Flutter\'s `Hero`: a tag (`"hero": "avatar-\${item.id}"`) flies the node from its place on the screen a\nnavigation leaves to the node with the same tag on the screen it opens; `flightShuttle` picks what flies (`morph`,\n`containerTransform`...). With `"flies": "inPlace"` it flies when it appears instead, from where the node with its\ntag was a moment ago on screen (a picked emoji flying from its picker to its chip, a card dropped into a column):\n`{"hero": {"tag": "react", "flies": "inPlace", "flight": {"duration": 720, "lift": 110}}}`, on a spring without a\n`flight`.'),
      DocSection('animation-clocks-and-game-loops', 'Clocks and game loops', 'A canvas\'s `timer` trigger (`"intervalMs": 1000`, `"when"`: a formula that must hold) runs every interval\n(`\${result.tick}` counts); `frame` runs every frame while `when` holds (`\${result.dt}` ms since the last), for\nphysics and game loops. Keep the state in variables and the work in a script when it has several steps.\n\nA clock written by a timer (`"value": "\${= now()}"`) changes in every capture. To check a countdown\'s states, pin\nthe time with the render command\'s `--now 2026-11-13T09:00:00Z` (`now()` returns it, so the timer writes it); a\n`--set clock=...` also holds against the timer for the capture. No test-only variable is needed.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'components',
    title: 'Components and sections',
    summary: 'Splitting a page into parts, each a file: a component used in several places with different values (a card, a chip, a row), a section used once (a header, a hero, an FAQ), their parameters (every kind, `variable` included), slots and events, the site manifest, and when to use a component, a list template or a section.',
    when: 'Splitting a page into parts, each a file: a component used in several places with different values (a card, a\nchip, a row), a section used once (a header, a hero, an FAQ), their parameters (every kind, `variable` included),\nslots and events, the site manifest, and when to use a component, a list template or a section.',
    example: 'A definition (`components/Chip.json`; the file is named after the type):\n\n```json\n{"schema": 3, "id": "Chip", "roots": ["chip"],\n "widget": {"type": "Chip", "doc": "A label with a remove button.", "children": "list", "slots": ["leading"],\n   "props": [\n     {"key": "label", "type": {"kind": "string", "flutter": "String"}, "default": "Chip", "required": true},\n     {"key": "selected", "type": {"kind": "variable", "of": {"kind": "boolean", "flutter": "bool"}}, "default": ""}],\n   "events": [{"key": "onRemove", "payload": {"kind": "string", "flutter": "String"}}]},\n "variables": {"chip": [{"name": "hovered", "type": "boolean", "value": false}]},\n "previews": [{"name": "Selected", "size": [240, 48], "props": {"label": "Design", "selected": true}}],\n "nodes": {\n  "chip": {"type": "row", "children": ["lead", "text", "extra", "remove"], "props": {"spacing": 6},\n           "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": 36, "padding": [12, 0, 8, 0]},\n           "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFE8EAF6"}], "radius": 18},\n           "bind": {"decoration.fills[0].color": "\${= props.selected ? \'#FF3F51B5\' : \'#FFE8EAF6\'}"},\n           "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"},\n                        "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "props.selected", "op": "toggle"}]}]},\n  "lead": {"type": "slot", "props": {"name": "leading"}},\n  "text": {"type": "text", "props": {"text": "\${props.label}", "style": {"fontSize": 14, "color": "#FF1A237E"}},\n           "layout": {"width": {"hug": 60}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n           "bind": {"props.style.color": "\${= props.selected ? \'#FFFFFFFF\' : \'#FF1A237E\'}"}},\n  "extra": {"type": "slot"},\n  "remove": {"type": "icon", "props": {"icon": "close", "color": "#FF5C6BC0"},\n             "layout": {"width": 20, "height": 20},\n             "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"},\n                          "actions": [{"type": "componentEvent", "event": "onRemove", "value": "\${props.label}"}]}]}\n }}\n```\n\nAnd calls to it, in a page\'s `nodes` (the page declares `tag` and `removed`):\n\n```json\n"nodes": {\n  "design": {"type": "Chip", "props": {"label": "Design", "selected": "tag"},\n             "slots": {"leading": "dot"}, "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": 36},\n             "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "event", "event": "onRemove"},\n                          "actions": [{"type": "setVariable", "variable": "removed", "value": "\${result}"}]}]},\n  "dot": {"type": "box", "layout": {"width": 8, "height": 8}, "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF4CAF50"}], "radius": 4}},\n  "tags": {"type": "listView", "children": ["tagChip"], "bind": {"data": "\${tags}"},\n           "props": {"scrollDirection": "horizontal", "spacing": 8}, "layout": {"width": {"fill": 360}, "height": 36}},\n  "tagChip": {"type": "Chip", "bind": {"props.label": "\${item.name}"}, "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"fill": 36}}}\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- A definition never reads its caller\'s variables: pass values as parameters, shared state as a `variable`\n  parameter.\n- A slot inside a list of the definition shows what the call passes once per item, built in the caller\'s scope:\n  it reads the caller\'s variables, not the item. To show the item, make it a parameter of a component the list\n  calls.\n- A call has no `decoration` and no `layout.padding` (`call_field_not_allowed`): style the definition\'s root.\n- The file is named after the type (`component_id_mismatch`).\n- `repeated_subtree` (an INFO) means the same subtree of three or more nodes is written several times over: make\n  it a component or a list template.',
    words: 3706,
    items: ['slot', 'external', 'placeholder', 'singlePlaceholder', 'event', 'componentEvent'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('components-parameter-kinds', 'Parameter kinds', 'Declared in `widget.props` as the catalog declares any prop: `key`, `type` (`kind` and the\nFlutter type; `min`, `max`, enum `values`, list `item`), `default`, `doc`, and `"required": true` for one a call\nmust set. The kinds: `boolean` (`bool`), `integer` (`int`), `number` (`double`), `string` (`String`),\n`enumeration` (with `values`), `value` (a value type: `{"kind": "value", "flutter": "Color"}`, also `EdgeInsets`,\n`Alignment`, `IconData`...), `list` (with `item`), `object` (a model: `TextStyle`, `Paint`), `json` (any data: a\nrecord, `{"kind": "json", "flutter": "Map<String, dynamic>"}`) and `variable` (with `of`, below). Inside, read them as `\${props.<key>}`. A call sets them as any node\'s props: a literal in `props`, an\nexpression in `bind` (`"props.label": "\${item.name}"`). Validation checks every call against the declaration:\nunknown keys, wrong types and bounds, missing required ones, children and slots the component does not take.'),
      DocSection('components-the-site-manifest', 'The site manifest', 'A directory with a `site.json` is a site: its pages, its components and its project variables, read by\nbare name in every page and component (a page or component variable of the same name is `duplicate_variable`).\n\n```json\n{"schema": 3, "pages": ["pages/home.json"], "components": ["components/Chip.json"],\n "variables": [{"name": "tags", "type": "list", "value": [{"name": "Design"}, {"name": "Code"}]}]}\n```\n\nWithout `components`, the files under `components/` are the site\'s components.'),
      DocSection('components-validation-codes', 'Validation codes', '`unknown_component` (a call to a type no definition declares),\n`duplicate_component`, `component_cycle` (a component calling itself, directly or through others),\n`component_id_mismatch` (the file is not named after its type), `invalid_component`, `missing_prop`,\n`unknown_event`, `call_field_not_allowed`, `slot_outside_component`, `root_placement_bound`. The render command\nadds `component_missing` (a call rendered without its definition: an empty box of its size).'),
      DocSection('components-triggers', 'Triggers', 'Written as `"trigger": {"type": "<trigger>", ...}` in a reaction ([trigger fields](interaction.md#interaction-trigger-fields)).\n\n| Trigger | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| <a id="trigger-event"></a>`event` | On a component call: the component fired its event `Trigger.event` (a `componentEvent` action inside its definition); `\${result}` is the event\'s payload. Flutter: the callback passed to a widget\'s `onChanged`-style parameter. The handler runs in the caller\'s scope. |'),
      DocSection('components-components-are-flutter-widget-classes', 'Components are Flutter widget classes', 'A page can be split into parts, each in a file of its own: a **component** is a document with one root (not a\ncanvas) and a `widget` declaration, and a page (or another component) **calls** it with one node whose `type` is\nthe component\'s type. A **section** is a component used once. The declaration is the widget\'s constructor; a\ncall is `PlanCard(price: 47, ...)`.\n\n| Here | Flutter |\n|---|---|\n| a component document | a `StatelessWidget` / `StatefulWidget` class, in its own file |\n| `widget.props` (parameters) | the constructor\'s named parameters, with types and defaults |\n| a call `{"type": "PlanCard", "props": {...}}` | `PlanCard(...)` in a parent\'s `build` |\n| `\${props.price}` in the definition | `widget.price` |\n| the definition\'s own `variables` (one set per instance) | the `State`\'s fields |\n| a `slot` node, the call\'s `children` / `slots` | `child`, `children`, `Widget title` parameters, placed in `build` |\n| `widget.events`, `componentEvent`, the call\'s `event` reaction | a `ValueChanged<T>` / `VoidCallback` parameter (`onChanged`) |\n| a `variable` parameter | a `ValueNotifier<T>` passed in |\n| `site.json` | the app\'s `lib/`: its pages and its globals |'),
      DocSection('components-a-complete-multi-page-site', 'A complete multi-page site', 'A site of two pages, a modal, a header and a footer shared by reference, written in the order that avoids\n`unknown_screen` errors: **the manifest first, every page listed**, then the components, then the pages. The trip\npage reads its route parameter (`\${route.id}`, from `navigate.params` or a link `trip?id=coast`); the saved list is\nrestored from storage when the home page loads; the packing list is kept per trip under a key built from the route.\n\n`site.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "pages": ["pages/home.json", "pages/trip.json"],\n  "components": ["components/Header.json", "components/Footer.json"],\n  "theme": {\n    "colors": {\n      "ink": "#FF1B1B1B",\n      "paper": "#FFFAF7F2",\n      "accent": "#FF2F6B4F",\n      "muted": "#FF6B7280",\n      "line": "#FFE5E1D8"\n    },\n    "textStyles": {\n      "body": {"fontSize": 15, "height": 1.4, "color": "ink"},\n      "title": {"from": "body", "fontSize": 28, "fontWeight": 700, "height": 1.2},\n      "link": {"from": "body", "fontWeight": 600, "color": "accent"}\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": [\n    {\n      "name": "trips",\n      "type": "list",\n      "value": [\n        {\n          "id": "alps",\n          "name": "The Alpine Arc",\n          "days": 7,\n          "packing": ["Rail pass", "Rain shell", "Walking boots"]\n        },\n        {"id": "coast", "name": "Coast to Coast", "days": 5, "packing": ["Swimwear", "Sun hat"]}\n      ]\n    },\n    {"name": "saved", "type": "list", "value": []}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`components/Header.json` (its About link opens the modal `about`, a canvas of `pages/home.json`; canvas ids are\nsite-wide, so any page or component may open it):\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "id": "Header",\n  "roots": ["bar"],\n  "widget": {\n    "type": "Header",\n    "doc": "The site\'s top bar: the name (home) and an About link (a modal).",\n    "props": [{"key": "savedCount", "type": {"kind": "integer", "flutter": "int"}, "default": 0}]\n  },\n  "nodes": {\n    "bar": {\n      "type": "row",\n      "children": ["brand", "count", "about"],\n      "props": {"spacing": 16},\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": 56, "padding": [20, 0, 20, 0]},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "paper"}], "strokes": [{"color": "line"}], "strokeSides": "bottom"}\n    },\n    "brand": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"hug": 22}},\n      "props": {"text": "Waymark", "style": {"from": "body", "fontWeight": 700}},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "navigate", "to": "home"}]}]\n    },\n    "count": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 120}, "height": {"hug": 22}},\n      "props": {"text": "\${props.savedCount} saved", "style": {"from": "body", "color": "muted"}, "textAlign": "right"}\n    },\n    "about": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"hug": 120}, "height": {"hug": 22}},\n      "props": {"text": "About", "style": "link"},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "openModal", "to": "about", "presentation": "dialog"}]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`components/Footer.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "id": "Footer",\n  "roots": ["foot"],\n\n(Continues: components.md#components-a-complete-multi-page-site.)'),
      DocSection('components-when-to-make-what', 'When to make what', '* **List template**: one shape repeated from data in one parent. When the item is more than about five nodes, or\n  appears elsewhere too, make the template one call node (`"bind": {"props.plan": "\${item}"}`).\n* **Component**: the same structure in two or more places with different values (buttons, cards, chips, rows),\n  or a part others will reuse. Data comes in as parameters. Four near-identical columns of a table, or three plan\n  cards, are one component (or one list template) called four or three times, not four copies.\n* **Section**: a top-level band of a page (header, hero, plans, FAQ, footer), in its own file when it is more\n  than about 15 nodes or someone will edit it alone, even if it is used once. Parameters only for what it shares\n  with its page (`variable` parameters for state both change).'),
      DocSection('components-what-a-definition-reads', 'What a definition reads', 'Its parameters (`props`), its own variables (one set per instance: two chips are\nhovered apart), the project\'s variables (`site.json`, below) and the runtime\'s scopes (`screen`, `route`,\n`theme`, `auth`...); inside its own lists, `item` and `index`. **Never the caller\'s variables**: the same chip works\non any page. What a section needs from its page comes in as a parameter.'),
      DocSection('components-computed-values-inside-a-definition', 'Computed values inside a definition', 'A definition\'s own variables may be computed from its parameters: `{"name": "over", "type": "boolean", "formula":\n"props.seats > props.limit"}` under the root\'s id in its `variables`, then `\${over}` in any of its nodes. One rule,\nread by five nodes, written once.'),
      DocSection('components-shared-state-variable-parameters', 'Shared state: variable parameters', 'share state with the caller: `{"kind": "variable", "of": {"kind": "boolean"}}`. The\ncall passes the *name* of one of its variables (`"selected": "tag"`); inside, `\${props.selected}` reads it live and\n`setVariable "props.selected"` writes it. A header and a menu both taking `"menuOpen": "menuOpen"` open and close\nthe page\'s one menu.'),
      DocSection('components-slots', 'Slots', 'A `slot` node in the definition is replaced by what the call passes: the call\'s `children` for the\nslot named `children` (the default name; declare `"children": "list"`), or the call\'s `slots[name]` for a named\nslot (declare it in `widget.slots`). With nothing passed, the slot shows its own children. What is passed belongs\nto the caller: it is stored in the page and reads the page\'s variables.'),
      DocSection('components-events', 'Events', 'Declared in `widget.events`; fired inside with `{"type": "componentEvent", "event": "onRemove",\n"value": ...}`; handled by the call\'s reaction `{"trigger": {"type": "event", "event": "onRemove"}}`, which runs in\nthe caller\'s scope with the value as `\${result}`. An event nobody handles does nothing.'),
      DocSection('components-size-and-place', 'Size and place', 'The call and the definition\'s root are one box: the call\'s `layout` sizes and places it\n(width, height, flex, margin, x/y, align, constraints); the root keeps its padding, decoration and contents. A call\nhas no `decoration` and no `layout.padding`. The root\'s own size is the design size its previews and new calls\nuse. `visible` hides the instance when either the call or the root is hidden. The root\'s own placement (its\n`margin`, `flex`, `align`, `x`/`y`, bound or patched) is not read: place the instance from the call (a margin that\ndepends on a parameter is bound on the call, `"bind": {"layout.margin": "\${= item.popular ? [0, 0, 0, 0] : [0, 28,\n0, 0]}"}`).'),
      DocSection('components-ids-and-paths', 'Ids and paths', 'A definition\'s ids are its own (`text`, `remove`); a page may use the same ids, and\ndiagnostics name a node of an instance by its path, so the two never mix. An action inside a definition that names\na node (`scrollTo`, `animate`, `focus`) acts on that node of its own instance: two cards each scroll their own\nlist. Tools name a\nnode inside an instance by its **path**: the call ids from the page down, then the node\'s id\n(`design/remove`, `plans/card1/cta`); `#n` picks the n-th copy a list repeats (`tagChip#2/text`).'),
      DocSection('components-rendering-one-part', 'Rendering one part', '`tool/render/render.sh site --out out --component Chip` renders the component alone, once\nper preview at its size; `--props \'{"label": "Long label"}\'` renders one parameter set at each size, and\n`--slots fixture.json` (`{"children": [ids], "slots": {"leading": id}, "nodes": {...}}`) passes slot content.\nSteps take paths: `--tap design/remove`.\n\n`--components-all` renders every component of the site that way in one run (`<Type>-<preview>@<w>x<h>.png`):\nthe quickest look at every part a page can call.'),
      DocSection('components-per-instance', 'Per instance', 'Everything a definition keeps is kept per instance, as a Flutter `State` is: its variables, its\ninteraction states, the values a `setValue` (or `setVariant`) sets on its nodes (set inside an instance, they change\nthat instance\'s node only). A variable with `"persist": true` is kept per instance path\n(`codelessly.component.<Type>.<path>.<name>` in the app\'s storage). When an instance leaves the screen (a list\nitem scrolled away, data that shrank), what it kept goes with it, as a `State` is disposed; shown again, it starts\nafresh (a persisted variable from its stored value).'),
      DocSection('components-published-components', 'Published components', 'A published site carries its components beside its pages (each at\n`publish/{project}/components/{Type}`, with a version and a digest; a bundle holds them in its `components` map),\nand an app loads the ones a screen calls with the screen, caches them, and follows a republished one: every\ninstance updates where it is, without reloading the pages that call it. Nothing to write in the app: a\n`CodelesslyWidget` showing a published site with components just works. A call whose component can\'t be loaded\nis an empty box of its size until it arrives (`component_missing` in the app\'s error log).'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'charts',
    title: 'Charts, gauges and indicators',
    summary: 'Showing numbers as pictures: progress bars and rings, activity spinners, badges, gauges, bar, line and series charts, scatter plots and barcodes.',
    when: 'Showing numbers as pictures: progress bars and rings, activity spinners, badges, gauges, bar, line and series\ncharts, scatter plots and barcodes.',
    example: 'A goal\'s progress as a bar bound to a variable, and a week as a bar chart:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["stats"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "stats": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 300},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["goal", "bar", "week"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 300}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "goal": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "\${done} of 7 days", "style": {"fontSize": 15, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "bar": {\n      "type": "progressBar",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 10},\n      "props": {"max": 7, "color": "#FF16A34A", "backgroundColor": "#FFE5E7EB", "borderRadius": 5},\n      "bind": {"props.value": "\${done}"}\n    },\n    "week": {\n      "type": "barChart",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 160},\n      "props": {\n        "values": [1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0],\n        "labels": ["M", "T", "W", "T", "F", "S", "S"],\n        "color": "#FF16A34A",\n        "labelFontFamily": "Roboto"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {"stats": [{"name": "done", "type": "integer", "value": 4}]}\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Chart colours default to a dark theme\'s; set `color`, `gridColor` and the label colours on a light page.\n- A `barChart`\'s labels default to JetBrains Mono: set `labelFontFamily` to a font you have (`font_fallback`).\n- A chart\'s size is its node\'s layout: give it a fixed height.\n- `value` above `max` is clamped.',
    words: 6561,
    items: ['progressBar', 'circularProgressIndicator', 'activityIndicator', 'badge', 'radialGauge', 'gaugeMeter', 'chart', 'barChart', 'lineChart', 'plotChart', 'barcode'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('charts-progress-from-state', 'Progress from state', 'Bind the value (`"bind": {"props.value": "\${done}"}`) with `max` the goal; `"animate": true` eases changes. A ring:\n`progressBar` with `"shape": "arc"` (`arcSweepAngle` 360 for a full circle) or `circularProgressIndicator`.'),
      DocSection('charts-charts-from-data', 'Charts from data', '`barChart` and `lineChart` take plain lists (`values`, `labels`); bind them to computed variables\n(`\${= map(week, d => d.count)}`). `chart` draws series over data rows (`data`, `series`, `labelField`) as bars,\nlines, areas, a timeline or a donut, with a selected index; `plotChart` plots x/y series with markers, ranges and\nreference lines.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'data',
    title: 'Data: APIs, cloud data, storage and form submission',
    summary: 'The `data` feature library: calling HTTP APIs, reading and writing the project\'s cloud documents and files, storing values on the device, and submitting forms.',
    when: 'The `data` feature library: calling HTTP APIs, reading and writing the project\'s cloud documents and files,\nstoring values on the device, and submitting forms. Not in the agent trust profile at run time (a host enables it).',
    example: 'A value saved on the device and read back as `\${storage.theme}`:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["prefs"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "prefs": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["saved", "save"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 200}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"crossAxisAlignment": "start", "spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "saved": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 20}},\n      "props": {"text": "Saved theme: \${storage.theme}", "style": {"fontSize": 15, "color": "#FF111827"}}\n    },\n    "save": {\n      "type": "filledButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 160, "height": 44},\n      "props": {"label": "Use dark", "style": {"backgroundColor": "#FF111827", "foregroundColor": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [\n            {"type": "setStorage", "key": "theme", "value": "dark"},\n            {"type": "showToast", "message": "Saved", "style": "success"}\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- These actions are not in the agent trust profile: a runtime model may document them but not use them unless the\n  host allows the `data` catalog.\n- An API\'s URL and secrets live in the publish model, never in the document.\n- `\${result}` is the response only inside `onSuccess`.',
    words: 2308,
    items: ['callApi', 'setStorage', 'cloudDocuments', 'loadCloudData', 'reloadCloudData', 'cloudFiles', 'cloudData', 'cloudBatch', 'submitForm'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('data-call-an-api-and-show-the-result', 'Call an API and show the result', '`callApi` names an API of the publish model (`services.apis`: method, URL, headers, body with `\${input}`\nplaceholders) and passes `params`; its result is `\${result}` in `onSuccess` (store it with `setVariable`), the\nerror in `onError`. Show a loading state with a variable set before the call and cleared in both chains.'),
      DocSection('data-cloud-documents', 'Cloud documents', '`cloudData` creates, updates, deletes, reads, queries or aggregates documents of a collection (`whereFilters`,\n`orderByFilters`, `limit`); its result goes in `resultVariable`. A list bound to a cloud query loads its pages\nthrough the list\'s `pagination`.'),
      DocSection('data-storage-on-the-device', 'Storage on the device', '`setStorage` writes `\${storage.<key>}` (a key may be a path into a stored map or list; `op` as `setVariable`\'s:\n`set`, `add` appends to a list, `insert` puts at an `index`, `remove` takes a value out). A variable with\n`"persist": true` is kept on the device too.\n\n- **Restore on load**: a canvas `load` reaction copies storage into a variable, `{"type": "setVariable",\n  "variable": "saved", "value": "\${= coalesce(storage.saved, [])}"}`; write it back after each change with\n  `{"type": "setStorage", "key": "saved", "valueType": "list", "value": "\${saved}"}`.\n- **A key per page or item** (a checklist per route): the key is an expression, `"key": "packed.\${route.id}"` with\n  `"op": "add"`, `"valueType": "list"`, `"value": "\${item}"`; read it with `\${= coalesce(get(storage.packed,\n  route.id), [])}`. A persisted variable is one value for every route.\n- The render command keeps storage in memory for one run: steps and `--navigate` see what earlier steps wrote; each\n  size and each run starts empty.\n\nA whole site using both: [a complete site](components.md#components-a-complete-multi-page-site).'),
      DocSection('data-submit-a-form', 'Submit a form', '`submitForm` validates the answers and stores them (`service: local`), or sends them to a destination the project\ndeclares; `onSuccess` and `onError` run after. See `docs/submit_form.md` in the package.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'auth',
    title: 'Auth: signing users in',
    summary: 'The `auth` feature library: signing app users in, up and out, and managing their account, with `\${auth}` to show who is signed in.',
    when: 'The `auth` feature library: signing app users in, up and out, and managing their account, with `\${auth}` to show\nwho is signed in.',
    example: 'A sign-in form whose error appears in a text:\n\n```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["signIn"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "signIn": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 320},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["email", "password", "error", "go"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 320}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "email": {\n      "type": "textField",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 56},\n      "props": {"decoration": {"labelText": "Email"}, "keyboardType": "emailAddress"},\n      "bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${email}"}\n    },\n    "password": {\n      "type": "textField",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 56},\n      "props": {"decoration": {"labelText": "Password"}, "obscureText": true},\n      "bind": {"props.initialValue": "\${password}"}\n    },\n    "error": {\n      "type": "text",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": {"hug": 18}},\n      "props": {"text": "\${authError}", "style": {"fontSize": 13, "color": "#FFDC2626"}},\n      "bind": {"visible": "\${= authError != \'\'}"}\n    },\n    "go": {\n      "type": "filledButton",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 48},\n      "props": {"label": "Sign in", "style": {"backgroundColor": "#FF2563EB", "foregroundColor": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [\n            {\n              "type": "auth",\n              "operation": "signIn",\n              "email": "\${email}",\n              "password": "\${password}",\n              "errorVariable": "authError"\n            },\n            {"type": "navigate", "to": "signIn", "mode": "pop"}\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  "variables": {\n    "signIn": [\n      {"name": "email", "type": "text", "value": ""},\n      {"name": "password", "type": "text", "value": ""},\n      {"name": "authError", "type": "text", "value": ""}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Not in the agent trust profile at run time.\n- Keep the password in a variable only as long as the form needs it.',
    words: 468,
    items: ['auth'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('auth-show-the-signed-in-user', 'Show the signed-in user', '`\${auth.isSignedIn}`, `\${auth.email}`, `\${auth.displayName}`, `\${auth.initial}`, `\${auth.role}` bind like any value: a header shows "Sign in" or\nthe user\'s name by `visible` bindings on `\${auth.isSignedIn}`.'),
      DocSection('auth-errors', 'Errors', 'A failure\'s message goes in `errorVariable` and stops the chain: actions after `auth` run only on success.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'commerce',
    title: 'Commerce: paywalls',
    summary: 'The `commerce` feature library: a paywall screen\'s interactions (buy, restore, select a product, close, open a legal link).',
    when: 'The `commerce` feature library: a paywall screen\'s interactions (buy, restore, select a product, close, open a\nlegal link).',
    example: '```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["upgrade"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "upgrade": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 200},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["buy", "restore"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 200}, "padding": 24},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "buy": {\n      "type": "filledButton",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 48},\n      "props": {"label": "Start free trial", "style": {"backgroundColor": "#FF2563EB", "foregroundColor": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "paywall", "operation": "purchase"}]}]\n    },\n    "restore": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 342}, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Restore purchases"},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "paywall", "operation": "restore"}]}]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Not in the agent trust profile at run time.\n- Prices shown must come from the store\'s products, not from text you write.',
    words: 439,
    items: ['paywall'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('commerce-a-paywall-screen', 'A paywall screen', 'The products and offers come from the project\'s paywall placement; the screen is an ordinary canvas whose buttons\nrun `paywall` operations (`selectProduct`, then `purchase`; `restore`; `closePaywall`; `openLegalLink`).'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'media',
    title: 'Media: video, audio, web views, speech and sound',
    summary: 'The `media` feature library: video players, embedded videos, an audio player, web views, reading text aloud, playing sounds, printing, capturing a screenshot, downloading a file and preloading images.',
    when: 'The `media` feature library: video players, embedded videos, an audio player, web views, reading text aloud,\nplaying sounds, printing, capturing a screenshot, downloading a file and preloading images.',
    example: '```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["watch"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "watch": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "col"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 320},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FF000000"}]}\n    },\n    "col": {\n      "type": "column",\n      "children": ["clip", "read"],\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": {"fill": 320}},\n      "props": {"spacing": 12}\n    },\n    "clip": {\n      "type": "video",\n      "layout": {"width": {"fill": 390}, "height": 220},\n      "props": {"url": "https://example.com/intro.mp4", "showControls": true, "fit": "cover"}\n    },\n    "read": {\n      "type": "textButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 200, "height": 40},\n      "props": {"label": "Read aloud", "style": {"foregroundColor": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "actions": [{"trigger": {"type": "click"}, "actions": [{"type": "speak", "text": "Welcome to the tour."}]}]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Not in the agent trust profile at run time.\n- The render command does not play media: a video draws its poster or nothing.',
    words: 1998,
    items: ['video', 'embeddedVideo', 'audioPlayer', 'webView', 'print', 'preloadImages', 'speak', 'playSound', 'captureScreenshot', 'downloadFile'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('media-control-a-player-from-state', 'Control a player from state', 'Bind `props.playing` and `props.positionSeconds` to variables to play, pause and seek from buttons; the player\'s\n`changed` trigger reports `ready`, `error`, the duration and the position.'),
      DocSection('media-save-a-file', 'Save a file', '`{"type": "downloadFile", "fileName": "trip.txt", "text": "\${brief}", "mimeType": "text/plain"}` offers the text as\na file (the browser\'s download, a save dialog elsewhere); `\${result.saved}` says whether it was saved. The keys are\n`fileName` and `text` (not `filename`, `content`). The render command saves it under `<out>/downloads/` and lists it.'),
      DocSection('media-read-along-text', 'Read-along text', '`speak` with `readAlong` times the words for a highlight bound to the spoken word.'),
    ],
  ),
  DocPage(
    id: 'engage',
    title: 'Engage: app events and automations',
    summary: 'The `engage` feature library: firing app events that the project\'s automations listen for (a popup after a lesson, a review prompt after the third order), and the `\${usage}` counters they read.',
    when: 'The `engage` feature library: firing app events that the project\'s automations listen for (a popup after a\nlesson, a review prompt after the third order), and the `\${usage}` counters they read.',
    example: '```json\n{\n  "schema": 3,\n  "roots": ["done"],\n  "nodes": {\n    "done": {\n      "type": "canvas",\n      "slots": {"body": "finish"},\n      "layout": {"width": 390, "height": 120},\n      "decoration": {"fills": [{"color": "#FFFFFFFF"}]}\n    },\n    "finish": {\n      "type": "filledButton",\n      "layout": {"width": 200, "height": 48},\n      "props": {"label": "Finish lesson", "style": {"backgroundColor": "#FF2563EB", "foregroundColor": "#FFFFFFFF"}},\n      "actions": [\n        {\n          "trigger": {"type": "click"},\n          "actions": [{"type": "emitEvent", "event": "lessonFinished", "props": {"lesson": "intro"}}]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```',
    pitfalls: '- Not in the agent trust profile at run time.\n- An event no automation listens for does nothing.',
    words: 311,
    items: ['emitEvent'],
    sections: [
      DocSection('engage-fire-an-event', 'Fire an event', '`{"type": "emitEvent", "event": "lessonFinished", "props": {"lesson": "intro"}}`: every automation of the project\nlistening for `lessonFinished` runs, reading `\${event.props.lesson}` and `\${usage.events.lessonFinished.count}`.\nAutomations live in the publish model, not in the document.'),
